00:12:14.416 --> 00:12:16.750
It's cool. We're good.

00:12:16.833 --> 00:12:18.458
No, I'm trying to be accountable here.

00:12:18.541 --> 00:12:22.916
I-I know that I have a bad habit of...

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:24.291
Charging ahead.

00:12:24.375 --> 00:12:25.666
It's not just you.

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:28.041
I've been kind of weird this week, too.

00:12:29.666 --> 00:12:30.666
Your dad.

00:12:32.208 --> 00:12:34.125
-Yeah. -Yeah.

00:12:34.208 --> 00:12:38.165
I know it's just that one backpacking trip he took here,

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.665
But I keep wanting to send him a picture...

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.583
[melancholy music playing]

00:12:42.665 --> 00:12:46.165
...or ask him what his favorite beach was or what kind of street food he ate.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:50.790
Just want to talk to him.

00:12:52.833 --> 00:12:56.125
We-we don't have to do the caves tomorrow if it's too much.

00:12:56.208 --> 00:12:57.708
No.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.583
That's the one thing I do know.

00:12:59.665 --> 00:13:02.166
He loved swimming in those caves.

00:13:03.708 --> 00:13:05.500
Tomorrow, Devil's Mouth.

00:13:06.958 --> 00:13:10.375
For your dad... and for all of us.

00:13:11.666 --> 00:13:12.791
[chuckles]

00:13:12.875 --> 00:13:15.833
You know, if you hadn't have charged ahead when he died,

00:13:15.916 --> 00:13:18.916
I probably would've left school.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.750
[Max] Mm.

00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:23.333
You basically wouldn't let me give up.

00:13:23.916 --> 00:13:25.666
Well, trauma sees trauma.

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:28.208
-Dead Parents Society and all that. -Yeah, yeah.

00:13:28.291 --> 00:13:29.500
Dragging me to those parties.

00:13:29.583 --> 00:13:31.208
Yeah. Questionable outfits.

00:13:31.291 --> 00:13:33.083
[both] Why were we always matching?

00:13:33.165 --> 00:13:34.875
Always matching. [laughs]

00:13:34.958 --> 00:13:37.790
Okay, the point is you saved me.

00:13:40.708 --> 00:13:42.165
It's real.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:45.665
Max magic.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.500
-Come on, say it. -No.

00:13:47.583 --> 00:13:48.583
Say it.

00:13:48.665 --> 00:13:50.208
-Only if you leave me alone. -Never.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.290
You and me...

00:13:52.625 --> 00:13:53.833
Till the stars burn out.

00:13:53.915 --> 00:13:55.875
Yes! Yes! That a girl.

00:13:55.958 --> 00:13:57.458
-[Max laughs] -[Adrienne squeals]

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.833
-Come on, skinny-dipping! [squeals] -Skin-- Oh!

00:13:59.915 --> 00:14:01.041
-Hell yeah. Hell yeah. -[Adrienne squeals]

00:14:01.125 --> 00:14:02.125
Oh, my God.

00:14:02.916 --> 00:14:05.333
-Come on. -No, no, I'm good.

00:14:05.416 --> 00:14:06.416
I'm good here.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:08.250
Oh, shit. Sorry.

00:14:08.333 --> 00:14:10.083
Uh... you know what?

00:14:10.166 --> 00:14:12.000
Never mind. You know what? They can do it.

00:14:12.083 --> 00:14:13.875
-Uh, but let-- -No. Seriously.

00:14:13.958 --> 00:14:17.041
James and Greg can be naked together.

00:14:17.125 --> 00:14:18.208
It's what they want.

00:14:18.291 --> 00:14:20.750
You guys go, please. I'm gonna be upset if you don't go, okay?

00:14:20.833 --> 00:14:21.833
Just go have fun.

00:14:21.916 --> 00:14:23.958
-Go, go, go, go, go, go! -[Adrienne] Okay!

00:14:24.041 --> 00:14:26.041
[Max and Adrienne whooping]

00:14:26.125 --> 00:14:27.750
[Adrienne] Skinny-dipping!

00:14:27.833 --> 00:14:29.583
[whooping, shouting]

00:14:29.666 --> 00:14:32.165
-[James] Hustle, hustle, hustle. -[Greg] Let's go, man. Hustle over here.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.540
[James] Take it off, take it off.

00:14:37.333 --> 00:14:39.000
-Get over here! -[Greg] Let's go, babe!

00:14:39.083 --> 00:14:41.083
[plaintive music playing]

00:14:42.083 --> 00:14:44.250
[squealing, laughter]

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:47.833
Whoo!

00:14:48.958 --> 00:14:50.750
[grunting]

00:14:50.833 --> 00:14:52.958
[leaves rustling in wind]

00:15:04.125 --> 00:15:05.666
-[Max screaming] -[James] What? What?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:06.708
What? What? What was it?

00:15:06.791 --> 00:15:08.666
I-I felt something. I felt... I felt something.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.583
-Oh, my God! I felt something! -[jarring, intense music playing]

00:15:10.666 --> 00:15:12.041
Go! Go!

00:15:13.125 --> 00:15:14.791
[panting]

00:15:20.041 --> 00:15:21.583
What--

00:15:21.666 --> 00:15:23.333
No, no, I-I felt something. I felt something.

00:15:23.416 --> 00:15:24.541
-What was it? -[Max stammers]

00:15:25.166 --> 00:15:26.500
There, there, there. What's that?

00:15:26.583 --> 00:15:28.833
The thing that just rolled up on the beach, washed up.

00:15:28.916 --> 00:15:31.000
[tense music playing]

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:41.500
[James] Whoa.

00:15:41.583 --> 00:15:42.958
[Adrienne] Is that a bite?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.500
Okay, this is the opposite of fun. Okay, so delete, delete, delete.

00:15:45.583 --> 00:15:48.333
Let's-let's just go back, and the van picks us up at 9:00 a.m.

00:15:48.415 --> 00:15:49.415
Eight, babe.

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:50.915
Okay, I said 8:00.

00:15:52.165 --> 00:15:54.083
Okay, it's freshwater stuff only tomorrow.

00:15:54.165 --> 00:15:56.000
It's nothing to be scared about.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.500
Come on, Sara. It's okay.

00:16:09.125 --> 00:16:11.750
[rousing music playing]

00:16:29.208 --> 00:16:31.208
♪ ♪

00:16:37.165 --> 00:16:39.625
[James] Wow.

00:16:39.708 --> 00:16:43.290
This is insane.

00:16:43.375 --> 00:16:45.083
[Adrienne] Oh, cool. Is that it?

00:16:45.165 --> 00:16:46.165
-What? -The Devil's Mouth.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.415
You see how the teeth are, like, reflecting in the water?

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:49.500
[Sara] Not yet.

00:16:49.583 --> 00:16:52.625
And if it's anything like the photos online, it's way more impressive.

00:16:52.708 --> 00:16:54.083
And way far away.

00:16:54.165 --> 00:16:57.165
Sh-Should we have packed more snacks?

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:00.041
I bet Sara has a protein bar in that backpack.

00:17:00.125 --> 00:17:02.041
-You bet I do. -[laughter]

00:17:02.125 --> 00:17:05.958
Don't come for me if you need snacks or emergency supplies.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:09.040
Okay? And I promise you guys, Devil's Mouth is gonna be worth the wait.

00:17:09.125 --> 00:17:10.415
And yes, this is also waterproof.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.165
Oh, you think of everything.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:13.750
Yeah, blame my Boy Scout brothers.

00:17:13.833 --> 00:17:15.040
Always be prepared.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.500
[camera clicks]

00:17:18.583 --> 00:17:19.583
Cute.

00:17:19.665 --> 00:17:21.665
♪ ♪

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:28.958
-[Adrienne] Hello. -Hello.

00:17:29.041 --> 00:17:30.541
Hi!

00:17:30.625 --> 00:17:31.666
There he is.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.208
[speaks Thai]

00:17:33.291 --> 00:17:36.125
My name is Wat. I will be your cave guide today.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.375
So, has anyone been in caves before?

00:17:39.958 --> 00:17:40.958
No?

00:17:41.041 --> 00:17:43.875
We're all cave virgins. Nice.

00:17:43.958 --> 00:17:47.041
And does anyone have fear of water or of swimming?

00:17:48.083 --> 00:17:50.500
I'm not afraid of the water, just what might be in it.

00:17:50.583 --> 00:17:51.583
[Wat] Don't worry.

00:17:51.666 --> 00:17:54.583
Uh, water is never more than ten, 15 meters deep.

00:17:54.666 --> 00:17:57.166
And maybe some small fish, like Finding Nemo.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.833
-[gasps] That's my comfort movie. -That's my comfort movie.

00:17:59.916 --> 00:18:02.916
[quiet, indistinct chatter]

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.625
I'll be fine.

00:18:04.708 --> 00:18:05.958
Just keep swimming.

00:18:06.041 --> 00:18:08.541
Well, we swim later. Now we kayak, okay?

00:18:08.625 --> 00:18:11.083
[grunting] Okay. Okay.

00:18:11.166 --> 00:18:13.083
-All right. -Whoa.

00:18:13.166 --> 00:18:15.375
[rousing music playing]

00:18:15.458 --> 00:18:16.791
[whooping]

00:18:16.875 --> 00:18:18.458
[Max] Oh, my God!

00:18:23.708 --> 00:18:25.500
[whooping]

00:18:29.208 --> 00:18:31.208
[whooping]

00:18:33.083 --> 00:18:34.750
[laughter]

00:18:40.458 --> 00:18:41.875
Wow.

00:18:43.458 --> 00:18:45.541
[whooping]

00:18:47.166 --> 00:18:49.125
[chuckles] My mom is gonna love these.

00:18:49.208 --> 00:18:51.458
Greg, you mention your mom one more time...

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.583
-[imitates cat growling] -[chuckles]

00:18:53.666 --> 00:18:55.000
[laughing]

00:18:55.083 --> 00:18:56.833
-[whooping] -[James] Yeah!

00:18:56.916 --> 00:18:59.791
[whooping]

00:19:01.375 --> 00:19:03.708
[Greg] Very nice! Very nice!

00:19:03.791 --> 00:19:05.166
[Max] So this is it?

00:19:06.375 --> 00:19:08.375
-This is cave entrance. -Oh.

00:19:08.458 --> 00:19:10.000
Not Devil's Mouth.

00:19:10.083 --> 00:19:11.916
It coming.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.583
-Look at that. -[Sara groans]

00:19:13.666 --> 00:19:15.208
[Sara hisses in pain]

00:19:15.291 --> 00:19:17.208
-You okay? -Yeah.

00:19:17.875 --> 00:19:19.333
Okay. All right.

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:22.166
-[camera clicks] -[laughter]

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:24.500
-Cute. -Super.

00:19:24.583 --> 00:19:26.791
[Adrienne] If you go into a cave and you don't make a TikTok about it,

00:19:26.875 --> 00:19:28.250
Did it even happen?

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.333
-It happened. -Um, hey.

00:19:30.416 --> 00:19:32.416
Handsome diver, four o'clock.

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:34.458
[quiet chatter]

00:19:35.708 --> 00:19:37.625
[Wat] Okay, guys.

00:19:37.708 --> 00:19:40.458
If you have any problems, please do not panic.

00:19:41.208 --> 00:19:42.416
-Just come tell me. -[James groans]

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:43.541
-Sorry. -Ow.

00:19:43.625 --> 00:19:46.500
So, today, we are going to take this Green Path here,

00:19:46.583 --> 00:19:48.541
Like you requested, Sara. Easy.

00:19:48.625 --> 00:19:51.166
Oh, but this looks cool, though.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.958
Maybe we try the Red Path.

00:19:53.041 --> 00:19:54.125
[chuckles] No, no, no.

00:19:54.208 --> 00:19:57.458
Uh, early monsoon already flood Red Path.

00:19:57.541 --> 00:19:58.791
Better for scuba.

00:19:58.875 --> 00:20:01.583
Thought monsoon season didn't start for another month, right?

00:20:01.666 --> 00:20:03.875
We had worst storm just a few days ago.

00:20:03.958 --> 00:20:05.708
But everything beautiful now, right?

00:20:05.791 --> 00:20:07.333
[Max clearing throat]

00:20:07.416 --> 00:20:11.625
Uh, I heard that the Red Path is also pretty cool.

00:20:11.708 --> 00:20:14.375
-Yeah, personally, I'm a big fan of red. -[Adrienne] Yeah, you are, baby.

00:20:14.458 --> 00:20:19.208
Okay, well, I read that the Green Path is just as cool and it's slightly easier.

00:20:19.291 --> 00:20:21.625
Yes, uh, Red Path is too hard.

00:20:21.708 --> 00:20:24.458
Too hard? Oh, my God, then we must.

00:20:24.541 --> 00:20:25.541
Hello.

00:20:26.708 --> 00:20:28.291
-I'm Max. [kisses] -Hi.

00:20:28.375 --> 00:20:29.583
-Nice to meet you. [kisses] -Okay.

00:20:29.666 --> 00:20:32.375
I'm the CEO of fun, so let's have a little fun, shall we?

00:20:32.458 --> 00:20:34.208
[Wat] Uh... uh...

00:20:34.291 --> 00:20:35.875
[chuckles] Uh...

00:20:37.375 --> 00:20:39.458
O-Okay. [laughs] Sounds good.

00:20:39.541 --> 00:20:43.875
Um, we can take Red Path, if that's okay with you, Sara.

00:20:44.875 --> 00:20:45.875
[chuckles softly]

00:20:48.541 --> 00:20:50.000
Of course.

00:20:50.083 --> 00:20:52.458
-Yeah, Sara. -[Max] Yeah.

00:20:52.541 --> 00:20:55.541
Watch out. Redhead on the Red Path.

00:20:55.625 --> 00:20:56.750
[Max] We so fun.

00:20:56.833 --> 00:20:59.875
Uh, life jacket is optional, but I would say you should--

00:20:59.958 --> 00:21:01.250
-Oh, I'll take one. -Okay.

00:21:01.333 --> 00:21:03.125
Thank you.

00:21:03.208 --> 00:21:04.958
-Here you go. -Thanks.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.500
Hey. Did the, uh... did the loud one do that to you?

00:21:10.583 --> 00:21:12.958
Like, just blink twice if you need help.

00:21:13.041 --> 00:21:16.041
Uh... pissed off some jellyfish.

00:21:16.125 --> 00:21:17.125
-Oh. -Mm.

00:21:17.208 --> 00:21:18.958
I've done the whole cave system back here.

00:21:19.041 --> 00:21:22.166
The worst thing I've ever seen is a really fat, depressed catfish.

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:23.333
Not pretty.

00:21:23.416 --> 00:21:24.416
Good to know.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:25.916
You know, we're lucky to get in here.

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:27.875
It's been closed down for a while 'cause of the storm surge.

00:21:27.958 --> 00:21:29.208
-Oh. -Yeah, today's the last day

00:21:29.291 --> 00:21:30.583
Before they shut down for Songkran.

00:21:30.666 --> 00:21:32.375
Thai New Year. Right.

00:21:32.458 --> 00:21:34.875
If you ever get scared out there, just look down, all right?

00:21:34.958 --> 00:21:36.375
I'll wink back up at you.

00:21:36.458 --> 00:21:37.791
See you.

00:21:40.666 --> 00:21:42.791
Were you guys just comparing whistle brands?

00:21:42.875 --> 00:21:45.458
-[inhales sharply] Something like that. -Ah.

00:21:45.541 --> 00:21:46.875
-Wedding's in the fall. -Right.

00:21:46.958 --> 00:21:48.166
-Small, intimate. -Cool.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.458
-Scuba-themed, obviously. -Mm-hmm.

00:21:50.541 --> 00:21:52.458
[Max] Hey, you two.

00:21:52.541 --> 00:21:54.125
-It's now or never. -[James] Okay.

00:21:54.208 --> 00:21:55.875
-All right. -Let's go.

00:21:55.958 --> 00:21:58.375
I'm just gonna get my stuff together.

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:04.125
[mysterious music playing]

00:22:10.791 --> 00:22:12.500
[Max and Adrienne whooping]

00:22:13.625 --> 00:22:14.916
[whooping]

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:16.041
Come on.

00:22:16.125 --> 00:22:17.916
Be like Greg. Don't think about it.

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:19.750
Yeah, I never think.

00:22:19.833 --> 00:22:21.708
[whooping]

00:22:25.291 --> 00:22:27.458
No jellyfish. I promise.

00:22:33.041 --> 00:22:34.041
[chuckling]

00:22:38.541 --> 00:22:39.791
-[tense music playing] -[screams]

00:22:39.875 --> 00:22:42.208
Whoa, what is it? What's the matter? What is it? What's wrong?

00:22:42.291 --> 00:22:43.916
-[breathing heavily] -[Wat] Sara, you okay?

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.125
An eel.

00:22:45.208 --> 00:22:47.041
Eels in ocean, not in cave.

00:22:47.125 --> 00:22:48.583
I saw it. I definitely saw it.

00:22:49.291 --> 00:22:50.875
Many things look like eel.

00:22:50.958 --> 00:22:53.250
[Greg laughing loudly]

00:22:53.333 --> 00:22:56.000
Greg, babe, please, no.

00:22:56.083 --> 00:22:58.125
-[laughing] 'Cause, you know-- -[James] Uh, don't. Don't finish it.

00:22:58.208 --> 00:23:00.041
Don't even finish the sentence.

00:23:01.333 --> 00:23:03.958
[faint, indistinct chatter]

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.666
[James] No turning back now.

00:23:07.666 --> 00:23:09.666
[mysterious music playing]

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:13.625
[quiet, indistinct chatter]

00:23:18.625 --> 00:23:20.625
[burbling]

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:29.625
[Wat] Next cave down Red Path is very special.

00:23:29.708 --> 00:23:31.500
You will see.

00:23:31.583 --> 00:23:33.083
But no noise.

00:23:33.166 --> 00:23:35.875
It is the Devil's Mouth.

00:23:35.958 --> 00:23:39.791
Pretty sure "the Devil's Mouth" is what the lacrosse team called Adrienne.

00:23:39.875 --> 00:23:41.500
Oh, you're just jealous.

00:23:42.916 --> 00:23:45.458
[Wat] Sara, I just wanted to tell you something.

00:23:45.541 --> 00:23:50.583
Before you go under, full exhale, then deep breath.

00:23:50.666 --> 00:23:51.875
Okay?

00:23:51.958 --> 00:23:53.958
[others chattering indistinctly]

00:23:59.250 --> 00:24:01.250
[atmospheric music playing]

00:24:25.791 --> 00:24:28.541
♪ ♪

00:24:28.625 --> 00:24:30.625
[indistinct chatter]

00:24:34.583 --> 00:24:36.375
[Wat] This is Blue Tunnel.

00:24:36.458 --> 00:24:38.541
Sunlight hits white sand.

00:24:38.625 --> 00:24:40.125
Shows us the way home.

00:24:40.208 --> 00:24:42.583
[Max] Tunnel means exit. Got it.

00:24:42.666 --> 00:24:44.666
[tranquil music playing]

00:24:46.916 --> 00:24:48.416
Wow.

00:24:52.125 --> 00:24:53.541
[Greg] This is the coolest cave ever.

00:24:53.625 --> 00:24:55.541
Shh.

00:24:55.625 --> 00:24:57.666
-[James] S-Sorry. -[Greg] Sorry.

00:24:59.166 --> 00:25:00.625
-[thuds] -Ow.

00:25:00.708 --> 00:25:02.208
Freaking Red Path.

00:25:04.583 --> 00:25:06.583
[mysterious music playing]

00:25:11.291 --> 00:25:12.708
[James] Whoa.

00:25:12.791 --> 00:25:14.083
[Max] Wow.

00:25:14.166 --> 00:25:16.416
This is Devil's Mouth.

00:25:16.500 --> 00:25:18.041
See?

00:25:18.125 --> 00:25:19.250
Teeth.

00:25:21.916 --> 00:25:23.916
[bats squeaking]

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.000
[wings fluttering]

00:25:44.083 --> 00:25:45.500
-[wings fluttering] -[screams]

00:25:45.583 --> 00:25:47.375
[bats squeaking]

00:25:47.458 --> 00:25:48.916
[Wat] Shh.

00:25:50.541 --> 00:25:52.541
[quiet, indistinct chatter]

00:25:57.583 --> 00:25:59.375
[whistles]

00:25:59.458 --> 00:26:02.458
-[bats squeaking frantically] -[dramatic music playing]

00:26:13.250 --> 00:26:14.708
Sara, hurry.

00:26:15.375 --> 00:26:17.250
Kind of cool, actually.

00:26:20.416 --> 00:26:22.166
[gasps]

00:26:22.250 --> 00:26:24.166
Wait, Max. [grunts]

00:26:24.250 --> 00:26:25.416
[tense music playing]

00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:27.625
[grunts, breathes heavily]

00:26:39.166 --> 00:26:40.791
[sighs]

00:26:42.958 --> 00:26:45.000
Ah, Sara, you okay?

00:26:45.083 --> 00:26:46.083
Yeah, I'm good.

00:26:46.166 --> 00:26:48.916
This is the Skeleton Cave.

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:50.833
Real bones below.

00:26:50.916 --> 00:26:52.625
Human? Animal?

00:26:52.708 --> 00:26:54.083
-Yes. Human. -[James clears throat]

00:26:54.166 --> 00:26:56.166
-Wat. -Yes?

00:26:56.250 --> 00:26:58.666
-You said "human bones." -Mm-hmm.

00:26:58.750 --> 00:27:00.291
What? Why?

00:27:00.375 --> 00:27:02.375
These caves, they're very old.

00:27:03.416 --> 00:27:04.625
Many, many years.

00:27:04.708 --> 00:27:07.291
Sinkhole and boom.

00:27:07.375 --> 00:27:09.125
Whole village die.

00:27:09.208 --> 00:27:11.291
We are guests here.

00:27:11.375 --> 00:27:13.333
Caves are master.

00:27:13.416 --> 00:27:14.833
If you do not respect the caves--

00:27:14.916 --> 00:27:17.416
James, the bone cave?

00:27:17.500 --> 00:27:18.916
-Get it, bro? -[Wat] Hey.

00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.583
-[laughing] The bone cave? -[Wat] Hey.

00:27:20.666 --> 00:27:22.708
This is no joke.

00:27:22.791 --> 00:27:24.791
[quiet, indistinct chatter]

00:27:27.375 --> 00:27:29.375
[Max] You okay? It's okay.

00:27:29.458 --> 00:27:30.958
God, James. Come on.

00:27:31.041 --> 00:27:32.291
Human bones.

00:27:32.375 --> 00:27:34.625
[Max] They're already dead. They're already dead.

00:27:34.708 --> 00:27:36.708
[mysterious music playing]

00:27:49.250 --> 00:27:51.250
-[Adrienne] Sara! We have an emergency! -[gasps]

00:27:51.333 --> 00:27:52.875
Emergency photo op.

00:27:52.958 --> 00:27:54.875
-[chuckling] -Come on.

00:27:54.958 --> 00:27:56.500
[Wat] Here. I'll take for you.

00:27:56.583 --> 00:27:58.041
[Greg] Start flexing, James.

00:27:58.125 --> 00:27:59.666
-[quiet, indistinct chatter] -[grunts]

00:27:59.750 --> 00:28:01.541
-[Wat] Okay, ready? -[Sara] Okay.

00:28:01.625 --> 00:28:03.833
One, two, three.

00:28:03.916 --> 00:28:06.000
[camera click echoes]

00:28:06.083 --> 00:28:07.083
[Max] Great.

00:28:07.166 --> 00:28:10.416
-Now we have Greg in our memories forever. -Yeah.

00:28:10.500 --> 00:28:12.708
-[Adrienne] That's funny, yeah. -[Max] Uh, I want you to shoot up.

00:28:12.791 --> 00:28:15.416
-[Adrienne] Okay. -[James] Phi Beta Kappa.

00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:18.041
You'd think he'd understand what "respect the caves" means.

00:28:18.125 --> 00:28:19.958
Ow. Greg, Greg!

00:28:20.041 --> 00:28:22.458
He should really point his toes more.

00:28:22.541 --> 00:28:25.291
-[indistinct chatter] -[Sara] Max, the director.

00:28:25.375 --> 00:28:28.500
-Taking charge since sophomore year. -Mm-hmm.

00:28:28.583 --> 00:28:30.666
How did we survive without her?

00:28:35.583 --> 00:28:36.916
-[grunts] -[others scream]

00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:39.708
Hey. What'd I tell you?

00:28:39.791 --> 00:28:41.291
This rock very weak.

00:28:41.375 --> 00:28:43.166
You cause collapse, we die.

00:28:43.250 --> 00:28:45.333
Yeah, yeah, I'm sorry. It was an accident.

00:28:45.416 --> 00:28:47.000
-I-I didn't mean to. -[snickers]

00:28:47.083 --> 00:28:48.125
[Wat] We go now.

00:28:48.208 --> 00:28:49.500
Next cave.

00:28:49.583 --> 00:28:50.666
[quiet laughter]

00:28:50.750 --> 00:28:52.625
Wh-What?

00:28:52.708 --> 00:28:54.708
Ooh, you got yelled at.

00:28:54.791 --> 00:28:57.666
[quiet, indistinct chatter]

00:28:57.750 --> 00:28:59.750
[foreboding music playing]

00:29:07.583 --> 00:29:09.583
[indistinct chatter continues]

00:29:13.958 --> 00:29:15.583
What is that?

00:29:15.666 --> 00:29:18.000
[James] What? What is it?

00:29:18.083 --> 00:29:20.166
[Greg] What's that smell?

00:29:20.250 --> 00:29:22.166
Ew.

00:29:22.250 --> 00:29:24.625
[Wat] These are saltwater fish from the ocean.

00:29:24.708 --> 00:29:25.875
[James] The hell?

00:29:25.958 --> 00:29:28.208
Uh, all these fish are dead.

00:29:34.625 --> 00:29:37.708
Baby, will you cancel our sushi plans tonight?

00:29:40.625 --> 00:29:42.458
How did they even get in here?

00:29:44.583 --> 00:29:47.750
[Sara] That cave opens to the ocean through that passage.

00:29:47.833 --> 00:29:48.958
[Wat] Yes.

00:29:49.541 --> 00:29:50.916
But the opening is very high.

00:29:51.750 --> 00:29:53.041
Too high.

00:29:53.125 --> 00:29:56.000
The storm could have flooded the ocean water in here.

00:29:56.083 --> 00:29:58.750
Then the fresh water killed all the sea life.

00:29:58.833 --> 00:30:01.166
Uh, should we turn around?

00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:02.666
[Wat] Uh...

00:30:03.833 --> 00:30:05.541
I take you back a different way.

00:30:05.625 --> 00:30:07.875
We go this way. Next cave.

00:30:10.458 --> 00:30:12.541
You okay?

00:30:12.625 --> 00:30:14.125
You can come with me.

00:30:14.208 --> 00:30:15.750
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:30:15.833 --> 00:30:17.791
Hey, Wat, what's with all the special attention?

00:30:17.875 --> 00:30:21.375
Uh, your friend, she tip extra,

00:30:21.458 --> 00:30:23.875
Say that you need extra care.

00:30:23.958 --> 00:30:25.166
I'm fine.

00:30:25.250 --> 00:30:27.458
I paid for the trip, so I'm the one who tips.

00:30:27.541 --> 00:30:29.166
No more special treatment, okay?

00:30:29.250 --> 00:30:31.250
-Okay. Yes. -Thank you.

00:30:33.833 --> 00:30:36.583
[others chattering indistinctly]

00:30:48.250 --> 00:30:50.250
[burbling]

00:30:53.375 --> 00:30:55.500
[tense music playing]

00:30:55.583 --> 00:30:57.166
[gasps] Geez.

00:30:57.250 --> 00:30:58.666
[exhales heavily]

00:31:05.125 --> 00:31:07.125
[ominous music playing]

00:31:20.333 --> 00:31:22.208
This is sick.

00:31:22.291 --> 00:31:23.625
Whoa.

00:31:26.208 --> 00:31:27.500
Wow.

00:31:27.583 --> 00:31:29.583
[quiet, indistinct chatter]

00:31:36.333 --> 00:31:38.333
-[Sara grunts] -[Max] How are the welts?

00:31:39.416 --> 00:31:41.958
Fine. Fresh water doesn't sting as much.

00:31:42.041 --> 00:31:44.375
-Yeah. -Is that why you put Wat on me?

00:31:44.458 --> 00:31:45.500
What?

00:31:45.583 --> 00:31:47.291
-He told me about your little tip. -Well, babe,

00:31:47.375 --> 00:31:49.791
You made such a big deal about me, like, not looking out for you the other day.

00:31:49.875 --> 00:31:50.875
I just thought--

00:31:50.958 --> 00:31:52.541
Pay someone to infantilize me?

00:31:53.916 --> 00:31:56.125
Sara, give me your knife.

00:31:58.666 --> 00:31:59.875
Gonna fight to the death?

00:31:59.958 --> 00:32:01.958
[others chattering indistinctly]

00:32:02.041 --> 00:32:04.041
[atmospheric music playing]

00:32:17.458 --> 00:32:18.916
-[Sara] Max. -[Max laughs]

00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:20.500
Now it's carved in stone.

00:32:20.583 --> 00:32:22.125
You're stuck with me. Boom!

00:32:22.208 --> 00:32:24.666
[muffled splashing]

00:32:24.750 --> 00:32:26.958
-Okay, cheeseball! -[Max laughing]

00:32:28.250 --> 00:32:29.958
Gay!

00:32:31.916 --> 00:32:33.583
-[screams] -What? What?

00:32:33.666 --> 00:32:36.000
I felt something on my fin.

00:32:36.083 --> 00:32:38.958
[breathing heavily]

00:32:39.041 --> 00:32:41.166
I don't see anything.

00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:44.416
Hey, uh, it's okay.

00:32:44.500 --> 00:32:47.083
-Yeah. -It's good. Come on, let's go.

00:32:47.166 --> 00:32:49.208
Hey, come on.

00:32:49.291 --> 00:32:50.708
It's okay.

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:03.625
Rocks are sharp. Go slow.

00:33:09.291 --> 00:33:12.708
It's amazing how old they are and still so fragile.

00:33:12.791 --> 00:33:15.083
Limestone sinkhole.

00:33:15.166 --> 00:33:17.541
-That's how the caves are formed. -[Greg] Limestone.

00:33:17.625 --> 00:33:19.333
Carbonate sedimentary.

00:33:19.416 --> 00:33:22.250
Let me guess: rocks for jocks?

00:33:22.333 --> 00:33:23.750
[laughing] You know it, baby.

00:33:23.833 --> 00:33:25.416
It's my first A.

00:33:25.500 --> 00:33:26.916
-[James] Uh... -Minus, minus.

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:37.000
[Adrienne whimpers]

00:33:37.083 --> 00:33:38.833
-Oh, damn. One of them cut me. -What's-- What--

00:33:38.916 --> 00:33:40.666
Oh, no, no, no, no, I can't look.

00:33:40.750 --> 00:33:41.833
Come on, come on.

00:33:41.916 --> 00:33:43.750
Oh, I can't look. I can't look. I can't look.

00:33:43.833 --> 00:33:46.625
There's damn knives all under us.

00:33:46.708 --> 00:33:48.791
Are you good, Cousin Greg?

00:33:48.875 --> 00:33:52.125
[Adrienne] Oh, oh, right. Uh, he has this thing about blood.

00:33:52.208 --> 00:33:53.958
Uh, babe, remember the mantra?

00:33:54.041 --> 00:33:55.500
-What's his thing about blood? -Yeah.

00:33:55.583 --> 00:33:56.791
He can't be around it.

00:33:56.875 --> 00:34:01.291
-"I am safe. I am special. I am me." -Yeah. Yeah. I'm me.

00:34:01.375 --> 00:34:02.916
Oh, my God, no.

00:34:03.625 --> 00:34:05.541
-No. -[James] Seriously, though, Greg,

00:34:05.625 --> 00:34:07.208
-you all right, bud? -Is it... is it done?

00:34:07.291 --> 00:34:09.333
Th-The blood, did she s-stop bleeding?

00:34:09.416 --> 00:34:11.083
[Sara] Can you guys calm him down?

00:34:11.166 --> 00:34:14.291
"I am safe, I am special, I am..." wh-whatever.

00:34:14.375 --> 00:34:16.375
[Greg] Well, when I was a kid, my brother pranked me.

00:34:16.458 --> 00:34:21.416
It was a fake bike accident with our neighbor Tanner, who was like five.

00:34:21.500 --> 00:34:23.500
-He used ketchup as blood. -[chuckles] Classic.

00:34:23.583 --> 00:34:25.291
Well, it totally traumatized me.

00:34:25.375 --> 00:34:27.916
Now, whenever I'm around blood, I-I... I panic.

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:29.208
Now all I see is dead Tan-Tan.

00:34:30.041 --> 00:34:32.250
[Sara] That tape should hold. Do you want to keep going?

00:34:32.333 --> 00:34:34.000
[Wat] No, no, no, no. Policy is,

00:34:34.083 --> 00:34:37.541
If any injury, we return, so we go back now.

00:34:37.625 --> 00:34:39.708
Okay, well, well, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:34:39.791 --> 00:34:42.541
Adrienne, babe, you're fine, right?

00:34:42.625 --> 00:34:44.583
Your concern for me is touching. It really is.

00:34:44.666 --> 00:34:47.708
I just read that the last cave is, like, a cannot-miss, you guys.

00:34:47.791 --> 00:34:49.000
Max, she is bleeding.

00:34:50.791 --> 00:34:52.791
Okay. How about this?

00:34:53.583 --> 00:34:56.625
You guys start going back, and I'm gonna go check out the cave really quick,

00:34:56.708 --> 00:34:58.666
And I'll swim really fast and catch up with you guys.

00:34:58.750 --> 00:35:00.375
You're gonna go check out the last cave by yourself?

00:35:00.458 --> 00:35:03.708
-Yep. -Wat, is that even safe?

00:35:03.791 --> 00:35:06.125
[Wat] No, no, no, not safe.

00:35:06.208 --> 00:35:08.208
[atmospheric music playing]

00:35:22.625 --> 00:35:24.625
[tense music playing]

00:35:35.208 --> 00:35:37.625
-[Max] Why shouldn't I do that, right? -[Adrienne] No, no, no. Hey, hey, hey.

00:35:37.708 --> 00:35:39.000
-What? -[Adrienne] I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:35:39.083 --> 00:35:43.458
Let's just go to the next one... together.

00:35:43.541 --> 00:35:44.583
Yay!

00:35:45.291 --> 00:35:47.541
[in Thai] Better get a good tip for this shit.

00:35:49.458 --> 00:35:50.625
[in English] Wh-What'd he say?

00:35:50.708 --> 00:35:53.458
All right, um, Greg. Hi, babe. Look at me.

00:35:53.541 --> 00:35:56.166
No more blood. Everything is okay.

00:35:56.250 --> 00:35:57.625
I am safe.

00:35:57.708 --> 00:36:00.041
-I am special. -I am special.

00:36:00.125 --> 00:36:01.333
[both] I am me.

00:36:01.416 --> 00:36:03.083
Okay, you assholes. All together.

00:36:03.166 --> 00:36:04.666
-I am safe. -[Greg] I'm safe.

00:36:04.750 --> 00:36:06.416
[Adrienne, Max and Greg] I am special.

00:36:06.500 --> 00:36:08.458
[Adrienne, Max, Greg and Sara] I am me.

00:36:08.541 --> 00:36:10.416
[atmospheric music playing]

00:36:10.500 --> 00:36:13.208
[Adrienne] Okay, this is it.

00:36:13.291 --> 00:36:15.958
-Better be worth it. -[James] I don't see anything yet.

00:36:21.708 --> 00:36:23.125
[Wat] Lights off.

00:36:23.208 --> 00:36:24.833
[Max] Guys, lights off.

00:36:24.916 --> 00:36:26.833
[James] Lights off, Greg. Lights off.

00:36:31.625 --> 00:36:34.041
-[laughing] Oh, my-- -What?

00:36:35.041 --> 00:36:36.708
Oh, my God.

00:36:36.791 --> 00:36:38.833
-[whooping] -No way.

00:36:38.916 --> 00:36:40.375
[laughter]

00:36:40.458 --> 00:36:42.375
Whoa. What?

00:36:46.083 --> 00:36:48.500
-[James] Whoa. -[Sara] Okay.

00:36:48.583 --> 00:36:50.458
Looks like the CEO of fun had a point.

00:36:50.541 --> 00:36:52.583
She is occasionally right, it's true.

00:36:52.666 --> 00:36:54.875
-You know I can hear you guys. -[Greg] Whoa, guys.

00:36:54.958 --> 00:36:57.458
Check it out. I'm freaking Harry Potter.

00:36:57.541 --> 00:36:59.666
[whoops, laughs]

00:36:59.750 --> 00:37:01.583
This is pretty epic, actually.

00:37:01.666 --> 00:37:04.750
-Yes! Yes! -I take care of you. I always do.

00:37:04.833 --> 00:37:06.875
[chuckling]

00:37:08.333 --> 00:37:09.958
[laughter, whooping]

00:37:11.625 --> 00:37:13.708
-[Greg] This is crazy. -[Wat] Okay.

00:37:13.791 --> 00:37:15.458
-We go now. -[Max] What?

00:37:15.541 --> 00:37:17.666
-No, we just got here. -I take you out longer way.

00:37:17.750 --> 00:37:18.750
More caves to see.

00:37:18.833 --> 00:37:20.291
Can we just chill here for a couple more minutes?

00:37:20.375 --> 00:37:21.791
My leg is kind of killing me.

00:37:21.875 --> 00:37:23.041
It-it's not bleeding, is it?

00:37:23.125 --> 00:37:24.208
Just two more minutes, okay?

00:37:24.958 --> 00:37:27.041
-[Greg chuckles] -[Max] Whee!

00:37:28.166 --> 00:37:30.041
[muffled laughter]

00:37:30.125 --> 00:37:32.125
[ominous music playing]

00:37:36.208 --> 00:37:38.291
How's the scrape, Ade? Do you want my life vest?

00:37:38.375 --> 00:37:40.041
You know what, actually, that would be amazing.

00:37:40.125 --> 00:37:42.208
-Okay. -Thank you. Yeah.

00:37:42.291 --> 00:37:44.916
[others chattering indistinctly]

00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:46.083
Here.

00:37:49.500 --> 00:37:51.333
Thank you.

00:37:54.208 --> 00:37:55.666
[inhales deeply]

00:38:06.833 --> 00:38:08.833
[tense music playing]

00:38:18.041 --> 00:38:19.541
[muffled shout]

00:38:20.958 --> 00:38:23.083
-[gasping] -[Adrienne] What? What? What happened?

00:38:23.166 --> 00:38:25.208
-What happened? -[Sara] The diver, he's hurt.

00:38:25.291 --> 00:38:26.708
-[Greg] Wh-What are you talking about? -[Adrienne] It's okay. It's okay.

00:38:26.791 --> 00:38:28.750
-Deep breaths. Deep breaths. -There's... there's so much blood.

00:38:28.833 --> 00:38:30.000
-You okay? -Like, bleeding?

00:38:30.083 --> 00:38:31.625
Babe, it's okay. It's okay. Hang on. Everything's fine. Just--

00:38:31.708 --> 00:38:33.458
-[Sara] Blood. -Okay, we need to leave now.

00:38:33.541 --> 00:38:35.666
But shouldn't we help him? Go down and look for him or something?

00:38:35.750 --> 00:38:36.916
I--

00:38:37.708 --> 00:38:38.916
[gasps]

00:39:00.500 --> 00:39:01.958
Chà-lam.

00:39:03.041 --> 00:39:04.541
Ch-Chà-lam? What does that mean?

00:39:05.958 --> 00:39:06.958
Chà-lam.

00:39:07.041 --> 00:39:09.125
Wh-What does that mean? What are you saying?

00:39:11.291 --> 00:39:13.375
-Shark. -[suspenseful music playing]

00:39:13.458 --> 00:39:15.083
[Sara, Adrienne and Max] What?

00:39:15.166 --> 00:39:16.000
-Shark? -In here?

00:39:16.083 --> 00:39:17.083
[Max] Wait, what are you saying? Wait, what are you--

00:39:17.166 --> 00:39:20.125
-What-what-what-- No. -[Adrienne] No! No, no, no, no, no!

00:39:20.208 --> 00:39:22.000
-[Max] Sara? -[Greg] You said shark?

00:39:22.583 --> 00:39:24.416
[Max] He said... he said... he said... you heard--

00:39:24.500 --> 00:39:27.041
-He said shark? You heard him say shark? -Yes, he said shark.

00:39:27.125 --> 00:39:28.583
-Just calm down. Calm down. -[overlapping chatter]

00:39:28.666 --> 00:39:30.000
Quiet!

00:39:30.083 --> 00:39:31.458
I don't know--

00:39:32.791 --> 00:39:35.250
Just, like, listen to Wat.

00:39:35.333 --> 00:39:36.708
We have to go now.

00:39:36.791 --> 00:39:37.791
-Okay. -[Wat] Okay?

00:39:37.875 --> 00:39:40.791
I'm sorry, how is there a shark in a freshwater cave system?

00:39:40.875 --> 00:39:42.875
Th-There are sharks that can do fresh and salt water.

00:39:42.958 --> 00:39:45.250
Okay, but how'd it get into a cave? Did it order a goddamn Uber?

00:39:45.333 --> 00:39:47.333
Guys, I don't think this is something we need to figure out right now.

00:39:47.416 --> 00:39:49.666
-Oh, I didn't call my mom today. -Look, just follow me, okay?

00:39:49.750 --> 00:39:50.958
-[Max] How do you know it's a shark? -Are you okay?

00:39:51.041 --> 00:39:52.041
-Okay, let's just go. -I'll be fine.

00:39:52.125 --> 00:39:53.166
-[Wat] We have to go. -Let's just go with Wat.

00:39:53.250 --> 00:39:54.291
Yeah, I'll go anywhere there's not blood.

00:39:54.375 --> 00:39:55.333
-We have to go. -[Sara] Let's go with him.

00:39:55.416 --> 00:39:56.541
-Wait. Wait, wait, wait. -Come on.

00:39:56.625 --> 00:39:57.958
Okay, I don't want to race through the caves

00:39:58.041 --> 00:39:59.458
If there's something dangerous out there, okay?

00:39:59.541 --> 00:40:00.541
What is the plan?

00:40:01.291 --> 00:40:02.666
I mean, it's a valid question.

00:40:02.750 --> 00:40:05.125
None of us should get in the water if we don't have a plan.

00:40:05.208 --> 00:40:07.125
I am the plan. I keep you safe. We go now.

00:40:07.208 --> 00:40:08.625
-Yes. -[Max] No, that's a bad idea.

00:40:08.708 --> 00:40:09.750
-No, no! -[Adrienne] Stop arguing, Max. Just--

00:40:09.833 --> 00:40:11.000
[Greg] Wait, that doesn't make s--

00:40:11.083 --> 00:40:12.791
-What-what if he doesn't come back? -[James] I don't think that's a bad idea.

00:40:12.875 --> 00:40:15.208
-[Max] I'm literally not gonna follow him. -He know... he knows what he's doing.

00:40:15.291 --> 00:40:17.500
No, forget him. I'm not going underwater.

00:40:17.583 --> 00:40:20.125
[overlapping arguing]

00:40:20.208 --> 00:40:21.291
Are you okay?

00:40:21.375 --> 00:40:22.375
[Max] Why would we go with him?

00:40:22.458 --> 00:40:23.708
-Why would we go in the water that-- -[Adrienne] Max, we--

00:40:23.791 --> 00:40:25.000
-[Sara] Are you serious? -Okay, follow me.

00:40:25.083 --> 00:40:27.708
-Hang on. Just one second. -I go now. Come if you want.

00:40:27.791 --> 00:40:30.208
[overlapping arguing]

00:40:30.291 --> 00:40:32.041
-I'm not leaving. -[arguing continues]

00:40:32.125 --> 00:40:33.416
Wat?

00:40:33.500 --> 00:40:35.125
-Wat? -[Max] No one is listening to me!

00:40:35.208 --> 00:40:36.541
No one is listening to me!

00:40:36.625 --> 00:40:39.291
-[overlapping arguing continues] -[tense music playing]

00:40:39.375 --> 00:40:41.375
-Wat! -[arguing stops]

00:40:44.500 --> 00:40:45.875
[Adrienne gasps]

00:40:46.666 --> 00:40:48.125
Oh, God.

00:40:48.208 --> 00:40:49.666
Oh, my God.

00:40:49.750 --> 00:40:51.458
Where'd he--

00:40:51.541 --> 00:40:53.125
What?

00:40:53.208 --> 00:40:54.583
He's gone.

00:40:56.250 --> 00:40:57.916
[Adrienne whimpers softly]

00:40:58.625 --> 00:41:00.958
No, no, no, no, this-this isn't... this isn't happening.

00:41:01.041 --> 00:41:03.000
It's not happening.

00:41:03.083 --> 00:41:04.916
I think it is.

00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:06.750
[foreboding music playing]

00:41:23.750 --> 00:41:24.958
[Greg] I'm gonna die.

00:41:25.041 --> 00:41:26.791
-I'm gonna die. I'm gonna die. [mutters] -Where the hell is Wat?

00:41:26.875 --> 00:41:28.916
Greg, buddy, you got to stop blubbering.

00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:31.916
Max, can you just please leave him alone?

00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:33.125
Are you sure you're okay?

00:41:33.208 --> 00:41:35.416
Yeah, it's just the tape's a little loose.

00:41:36.541 --> 00:41:37.875
All right, I'm gonna fix it.

00:41:37.958 --> 00:41:39.958
I'll fix it up there when we get out of the cave, okay?

00:41:40.041 --> 00:41:41.625
Okay, I just don't want to ask everyone to stop.

00:41:42.583 --> 00:41:44.833
We're all getting out of here-- together.

00:41:45.833 --> 00:41:47.833
[tense, atmospheric music playing]

00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:07.000
Greg?

00:42:08.166 --> 00:42:09.208
-Greg! -[Max] Shh!

00:42:09.291 --> 00:42:10.875
Do you want it to follow us?

00:42:14.083 --> 00:42:16.041
-Greg! -Shh!

00:42:16.125 --> 00:42:18.125
[Greg muttering, whimpering in distance]

00:42:25.375 --> 00:42:26.791
[James] Greg, buddy.

00:42:27.791 --> 00:42:30.291
[Greg breathing heavily] Oh, God, I can't... I can't breathe.

00:42:30.375 --> 00:42:32.083
I can't breathe.

00:42:32.166 --> 00:42:34.125
Oh, my God. Oh.

00:42:34.208 --> 00:42:36.708
Please. I'm s-- I'm sorry. Just-just-just leave me, okay?

00:42:36.791 --> 00:42:37.916
Just-just leave me alone.

00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:39.458
What are you talking about?

00:42:39.541 --> 00:42:41.791
We're counting on you to Aquaman our way out of this.

00:42:43.500 --> 00:42:45.125
-I love Jason Momoa. -Yeah.

00:42:45.208 --> 00:42:46.708
Yeah, you do.

00:42:46.791 --> 00:42:48.708
-Adrienne, can we borrow that life vest? -Yeah.

00:42:48.791 --> 00:42:50.958
Time to get our superhero back in action.

00:42:51.041 --> 00:42:53.375
Let's, uh... let's do it for Tommy, huh?

00:42:53.458 --> 00:42:55.458
-It's Tanner. -Tanner?

00:42:55.541 --> 00:42:56.583
-Yeah, Tanner. -Tan-Tan. Yeah.

00:42:59.916 --> 00:43:02.625
-All right, bud. Up and over. -[Greg muttering]

00:43:02.708 --> 00:43:05.000
Just relax. I got you.

00:43:05.083 --> 00:43:06.333
-All right, let's go. -Oh, God.

00:43:06.416 --> 00:43:09.250
-Let's get you out. -Oh, I... I didn't call my mom.

00:43:09.333 --> 00:43:11.291
I-I didn't call my mom.

00:43:11.375 --> 00:43:12.875
I should've called my mom.

00:43:12.958 --> 00:43:14.958
[tense, atmospheric music continues]

00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:28.208
[shuddering breaths]

00:43:39.583 --> 00:43:41.791
[suspenseful music playing]

00:43:46.708 --> 00:43:48.791
[screams]

00:43:52.041 --> 00:43:55.041
[gasping breaths]

00:43:59.333 --> 00:44:01.416
[screaming]

00:44:06.416 --> 00:44:08.416
[gasping breaths]

00:44:12.875 --> 00:44:14.416
[Greg gasping]

00:44:14.500 --> 00:44:16.375
[screaming]

00:44:16.458 --> 00:44:18.208
[screams] Greg!

00:44:18.291 --> 00:44:20.333
-[panicked shouting] -[head thuds]

00:44:21.500 --> 00:44:24.208
[indistinct shouting, screaming]

00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:28.958
[sobbing] Greg.

00:44:33.208 --> 00:44:36.041
[frantic shouting, screaming]

00:44:41.625 --> 00:44:43.875
[shouting and screaming stop]

00:44:43.958 --> 00:44:45.958
[shuddering breaths]

00:44:55.666 --> 00:44:57.083
[gasps]

00:45:03.125 --> 00:45:05.083
[screaming]

00:45:05.166 --> 00:45:06.541
[James] Come on, let's go!

00:45:06.625 --> 00:45:08.250
-[Adrienne] No, we can't leave him! -We have to go.

00:45:08.333 --> 00:45:10.750
-[James] Let's go! -[Adrienne] No, we can't leave him!

00:45:10.833 --> 00:45:12.208
No!

00:45:12.291 --> 00:45:14.291
[sobbing] No!

00:45:16.041 --> 00:45:17.500
[intense music playing]

00:45:17.583 --> 00:45:18.791
Come on.

00:45:18.875 --> 00:45:20.041
[heavy breathing, whimpering]

00:45:20.125 --> 00:45:21.125
James?

00:45:21.208 --> 00:45:22.583
-[Max] Come on. Go, go! -[James] Go, go. Sara, go.

00:45:22.666 --> 00:45:24.166
[Max] Come on, come on, come on, come on!

00:45:24.250 --> 00:45:25.875
[James] Come on, come on. Go, go, go.

00:45:25.958 --> 00:45:27.875
[frantic, indistinct chatter]

00:45:27.958 --> 00:45:29.916
[pained grunting]

00:45:31.000 --> 00:45:32.416
[Max] Okay. I'll push.

00:45:35.375 --> 00:45:37.541
[yells]

00:45:37.625 --> 00:45:39.625
[all breathing heavily]

00:45:42.625 --> 00:45:43.708
[Sara] Hey, hey, hey.

00:45:43.791 --> 00:45:45.833
Look, they're not even that bad, okay?

00:45:45.916 --> 00:45:48.500
-Hey, it's okay. Shh. -[gasping breaths]

00:45:48.583 --> 00:45:50.541
They're not even that deep. It's just...

00:45:50.625 --> 00:45:52.375
We're gonna just wait for the bleeding to stop,

00:45:52.458 --> 00:45:53.875
-and then we're gonna take you up. -No, no.

00:45:53.958 --> 00:45:56.083
Sharks can smell a drop of blood in the ocean. It's not gonna work.

00:45:56.166 --> 00:45:57.458
How did she get so beat up like this? I--

00:45:57.541 --> 00:46:00.375
The rocks, when she went under. It must have dragged her.

00:46:00.458 --> 00:46:01.458
[James stammering]

00:46:01.541 --> 00:46:03.416
So... so what do we do?

00:46:03.500 --> 00:46:04.958
We're gonna tape her up, okay?

00:46:05.041 --> 00:46:07.375
And then we'll get out of here.

00:46:07.458 --> 00:46:09.708
I-I can figure this out. I can. Just, like, let me think.

00:46:09.791 --> 00:46:11.625
Like, no one move, no one do anything crazy.

00:46:11.708 --> 00:46:14.041
-[shushing] -What? What?

00:46:16.791 --> 00:46:18.000
Bull shark.

00:46:19.083 --> 00:46:21.750
It has to be. That's what I was saying.

00:46:21.833 --> 00:46:24.666
They can do fresh and salt water.

00:46:24.750 --> 00:46:26.125
And they're aggressive as hell.

00:46:26.208 --> 00:46:28.666
They-they bash their prey with their head.

00:46:28.750 --> 00:46:31.375
-They go after you and after you. -[Adrienne laughing]

00:46:32.458 --> 00:46:35.125
[laughing] It's like a cartoon.

00:46:35.208 --> 00:46:38.625
It's like a guy wearing a fin hat on his...

00:46:38.708 --> 00:46:40.875
[sobbing] ...on his head.

00:46:40.958 --> 00:46:42.875
Oh, my God, Greg.

00:46:42.958 --> 00:46:45.416
He calls his mom every night.

00:46:45.500 --> 00:46:47.666
[continues sobbing]

00:46:47.750 --> 00:46:49.875
I-I... I don't understand how this happened, okay?

00:46:49.958 --> 00:46:51.625
This wasn't supposed to happen. This isn't supposed to--

00:46:51.708 --> 00:46:54.708
[James] It's-it's like it's-it's... it's stuck in this maze,

00:46:54.791 --> 00:46:57.083
And it's territorial and...

00:47:05.208 --> 00:47:06.666
[Sara] It's gone.

00:47:07.791 --> 00:47:09.500
[Max] I can't believe Wat left us.

00:47:09.583 --> 00:47:11.083
We weren't listening to him.

00:47:11.166 --> 00:47:12.583
Yeah, yeah, but he was in charge.

00:47:12.666 --> 00:47:14.916
Which is why we should've listened to him.

00:47:15.916 --> 00:47:18.250
Okay, well, Wat is faster than us.

00:47:19.583 --> 00:47:23.250
So he's gonna get out of here, and he's gonna send for help.

00:47:23.333 --> 00:47:25.125
And-and we have... we have to stay here,

00:47:25.208 --> 00:47:26.416
-and we're gonna wait. -Oh, God.

00:47:26.500 --> 00:47:27.708
It's the right thing to do. Okay?

00:47:27.791 --> 00:47:29.500
It's like when you're a kid and you get lost.

00:47:29.583 --> 00:47:32.041
You just stay where you are, and you wait and...

00:47:33.125 --> 00:47:35.500
Wh-What are you looking at?

00:47:35.583 --> 00:47:38.375
I'm trying to see where he might have gone.

00:47:38.458 --> 00:47:41.416
The dead fish cave is next, then there's the bat cave.

00:47:41.500 --> 00:47:43.708
-[Max] No. -And then we're so close.

00:47:43.791 --> 00:47:44.875
He could've gone this way.

00:47:44.958 --> 00:47:46.541
It's kind of like a honeycomb.

00:47:46.625 --> 00:47:48.958
They're super narrow tunnels, so maybe the shark couldn't follow.

00:47:49.041 --> 00:47:50.500
Oh, babe, it's a waste of time.

00:47:51.583 --> 00:47:52.708
What do you mean?

00:47:52.791 --> 00:47:54.958
Wat is gonna send for help, okay?

00:47:55.041 --> 00:47:56.166
It's as easy as that.

00:47:59.166 --> 00:48:00.583
What if he doesn't make it?

00:48:00.666 --> 00:48:02.708
Well, someone is gonna come for us.

00:48:02.791 --> 00:48:04.791
I... I promise.

00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:10.000
[water dripping]

00:48:36.333 --> 00:48:39.333
[taking deep breaths]

00:48:46.333 --> 00:48:48.333
[burbling]

00:49:01.625 --> 00:49:03.625
[tense music playing]

00:49:16.125 --> 00:49:17.708
[yells]

00:49:17.791 --> 00:49:19.083
[gasping]

00:49:19.166 --> 00:49:21.166
[intense music playing]

00:49:23.541 --> 00:49:25.541
-[grunts] -[splashes]

00:49:31.791 --> 00:49:33.791
[music stops]

00:49:35.833 --> 00:49:38.208
[gasping breaths]

00:49:45.208 --> 00:49:47.375
-[grunts] -[jarring, intense music playing]

00:49:50.458 --> 00:49:52.666
[screaming]

00:49:53.750 --> 00:49:55.208
[Max] No.

00:49:55.291 --> 00:49:57.208
No. No.

00:49:57.291 --> 00:49:59.166
No, no, no, no, no, no!

00:49:59.250 --> 00:50:00.916
[sobbing] No! No.

00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:02.750
-Oh, my God. -[Max] No.

00:50:03.833 --> 00:50:05.916
No one's coming for us.

00:50:06.000 --> 00:50:07.833
What-what-what... what do we do? What do we do?

00:50:07.916 --> 00:50:11.833
We figure out which of the two paths Wat took, and then we take the other one.

00:50:11.916 --> 00:50:14.458
-No, that's impossible. -Wait, wait. There is another way.

00:50:14.541 --> 00:50:16.375
We can get to the ocean in the next cave.

00:50:16.458 --> 00:50:17.833
-The ocean? -Yes, I saw the passage

00:50:17.916 --> 00:50:21.041
That leads to the hatch that opens to the sea.

00:50:21.125 --> 00:50:23.208
-Look. It's the shortest way. -[Max] Okay, just wait, wait, wait, wait,

00:50:23.291 --> 00:50:24.458
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:50:24.541 --> 00:50:25.916
We have a map to the caves.

00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:28.458
We do not have a map to the ocean, okay, so-- [stammers]

00:50:28.541 --> 00:50:31.750
W-We don't know where it's gonna spit us out in the ocean.

00:50:31.833 --> 00:50:34.375
There's a reason that the shark is stuck in here.

00:50:35.083 --> 00:50:36.083
No.

00:50:36.166 --> 00:50:37.750
-Adrienne. -[Adrienne whimpering] No.

00:50:37.833 --> 00:50:39.541
You're hurt and you're bleeding, and we have to

00:50:39.625 --> 00:50:40.625
-get you help. -No, Max, don't leave me.

00:50:40.708 --> 00:50:41.833
-You have to stay up here. -I'm not like you.

00:50:41.916 --> 00:50:43.125
No, Adrienne, that's what I'm saying.

00:50:43.208 --> 00:50:46.041
[sobbing] No, Greg is dead! He's dead, and you're all just...

00:50:46.125 --> 00:50:48.583
You're all just arguing, and he's gone.

00:50:48.666 --> 00:50:50.916
-I don't want to die here alone. -[James] Okay.

00:50:51.000 --> 00:50:54.041
Okay. Okay. Why don't we all just wait here?

00:50:54.125 --> 00:50:55.750
When someone realizes

00:50:55.833 --> 00:50:57.166
-Wat hasn't come back, we-- -[Max] It's a holiday.

00:50:57.250 --> 00:50:59.875
We're not gonna post up here and just wait for no one, James.

00:50:59.958 --> 00:51:02.541
I can stay with her, and... and you guys just go.

00:51:02.625 --> 00:51:04.458
No. I don't like any of this.

00:51:04.541 --> 00:51:06.541
We have to face the facts.

00:51:06.625 --> 00:51:09.083
Wat did this for a living, and he's dead, okay?

00:51:09.166 --> 00:51:10.916
So the three of us, we have to stick together

00:51:11.000 --> 00:51:13.375
So we can get help for Adrienne.

00:51:13.458 --> 00:51:15.208
[sniffling]

00:51:16.250 --> 00:51:18.083
I can't leave her.

00:51:19.166 --> 00:51:20.791
Fine.

00:51:20.875 --> 00:51:23.125
Then give me the map, because James and I are going.

00:51:23.208 --> 00:51:24.875
I don't think we should leave her, either.

00:51:24.958 --> 00:51:26.083
James.

00:51:26.166 --> 00:51:28.375
No, there's got to be a way that we can get help

00:51:28.458 --> 00:51:31.541
Without leaving one of our friends alone and bleeding.

00:51:31.625 --> 00:51:33.500
Then you two stay with her, but give me the map

00:51:33.583 --> 00:51:35.125
So I can save your asses.

00:51:35.208 --> 00:51:36.208
No.

00:51:36.291 --> 00:51:38.708
-No. No, Max. No, please don't. -Sara, Sara, give me the map.

00:51:38.791 --> 00:51:40.458
-Okay. -No, don't. No, no, no, no, no!

00:51:40.541 --> 00:51:42.541
Give it to me! Give it to me!

00:51:42.625 --> 00:51:44.125
-[screaming] -Adrienne!

00:51:44.208 --> 00:51:45.916
-Get out of the water! Come on! -[gasping]

00:51:46.000 --> 00:51:47.583
Get out of the water! Come on!

00:51:47.666 --> 00:51:50.250
[gasping, coughing]

00:51:50.333 --> 00:51:52.000
-Pull me up. Pull me up. -Hurry, hurry, hurry, hurry.

00:51:52.083 --> 00:51:54.250
-Pull me up. Pull me up. -[tense music playing]

00:51:54.333 --> 00:51:55.625
Help!

00:51:55.708 --> 00:51:57.750
Pull me up! Pull me up!

00:51:57.833 --> 00:51:58.833
Adrienne, hurry up!

00:51:58.916 --> 00:52:00.833
-[James] Reach. Reach. -[Adrienne] Okay, help me! Help me!

00:52:00.916 --> 00:52:02.708
-[sobbing] Help. -[James] Adrienne, grab my hand!

00:52:03.500 --> 00:52:05.250
[Adrienne] Pull me up. Pull me up.

00:52:06.875 --> 00:52:09.458
Come on, come on, come on. Adrienne, reach! Grab my hand.

00:52:09.541 --> 00:52:11.666
-[Sara] Come on, come on. -[James] Come on, come on.

00:52:12.875 --> 00:52:14.958
-[Adrienne screams] -[thudding]

00:52:15.041 --> 00:52:17.208
[screaming, whimpering]

00:52:17.291 --> 00:52:18.708
[James] Oh, God!

00:52:23.041 --> 00:52:25.000
It's stuck! It's stuck!

00:52:26.750 --> 00:52:28.208
If it can't swim forward, it can't breathe.

00:52:28.291 --> 00:52:30.041
Yeah, and it can't swim backwards.

00:52:31.875 --> 00:52:34.833
Ade, listen, I think we can go, but we've got to go right now.

00:52:34.916 --> 00:52:35.916
-No. -[James] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:52:36.000 --> 00:52:37.125
Adrienne, we will help you.

00:52:37.208 --> 00:52:40.041
-Okay, but we got to go right now, though. -Hey, hey, hey. Listen to me.

00:52:40.750 --> 00:52:44.458
I'll carry you the whole way, but you got to get back in the water.

00:52:47.000 --> 00:52:49.250
-[Max] Come on, let's go! -[Sara] I'll count us in. Let's go.

00:52:49.333 --> 00:52:51.166
-[Max] One at a time. One at a time. -[shouts frantically, screams]

00:52:51.250 --> 00:52:52.708
-[screams] -[James] No, Adrienne!

00:52:52.791 --> 00:52:54.791
[intense music playing]

00:52:57.083 --> 00:52:58.625
[Sara] All right, I'm-I'm coming.

00:52:58.708 --> 00:53:00.250
I'm coming!

00:53:00.333 --> 00:53:01.833
Get closer.

00:53:01.916 --> 00:53:03.333
I can't reach.

00:53:03.416 --> 00:53:04.583
Adrienne.

00:53:04.666 --> 00:53:06.250
Can you grab my hand?

00:53:06.333 --> 00:53:07.916
-Adrienne. -[Max] Look. Look.

00:53:08.000 --> 00:53:09.000
No.

00:53:09.833 --> 00:53:10.916
[James] Swim!

00:53:11.000 --> 00:53:12.000
-[screams] -[Sara] Hurry up!

00:53:12.083 --> 00:53:14.500
-Adrienne! Grab my hand! -Come on!

00:53:14.583 --> 00:53:15.708
[James] Grab my hand!

00:53:15.791 --> 00:53:17.458
-[screaming] -Grab it!

00:53:19.250 --> 00:53:22.166
[screaming]

00:53:35.250 --> 00:53:36.916
[screaming stops]

00:53:41.041 --> 00:53:43.500
[heavy, shuddering breaths]

00:53:45.458 --> 00:53:47.375
[voice shaking] This is so messed up.

00:53:48.875 --> 00:53:50.208
I... I can't...

00:53:50.291 --> 00:53:53.250
[voice shaking] How did-- She-she-she-she was--

00:53:53.333 --> 00:53:55.166
Gone.

00:53:55.250 --> 00:53:57.500
[somber music playing]

00:53:57.583 --> 00:53:59.583
[sobbing]

00:54:05.583 --> 00:54:07.625
[whimpers]

00:54:13.416 --> 00:54:14.916
[grunts]

00:54:15.625 --> 00:54:17.250
[whimpering]

00:54:24.500 --> 00:54:26.583
I've never seen anyone die before.

00:54:30.666 --> 00:54:32.625
Now I've seen two. [sniffles]

00:54:35.250 --> 00:54:36.541
We could've saved her.

00:54:36.625 --> 00:54:38.416
You would've died, too.

00:54:40.708 --> 00:54:42.916
We need to get out of here. This ledge is crumbling.

00:54:43.916 --> 00:54:46.000
-[Max whimpering] -The ocean outlet.

00:54:47.541 --> 00:54:48.958
The honeycomb caves.

00:54:49.041 --> 00:54:51.375
We have to go where it can't follow us easily.

00:54:51.458 --> 00:54:54.250
So maybe it'll get stuck again. Maybe it'll die.

00:54:54.333 --> 00:54:56.958
So the narrower the passage, the better, so--

00:54:57.041 --> 00:54:58.375
The less time we spend in here, the better.

00:54:58.458 --> 00:55:00.958
And the ocean is the closest way out, away from the shark.

00:55:01.041 --> 00:55:03.208
Do you know where the shark came from, Sara?

00:55:03.291 --> 00:55:04.458
The ocean, okay?

00:55:04.541 --> 00:55:06.916
And I'm willing to bet it's not the only one in there.

00:55:07.000 --> 00:55:08.791
But I think our odds are better out there.

00:55:08.875 --> 00:55:10.083
'Cause if we get attacked in here--

00:55:10.166 --> 00:55:11.458
But it can't follow us in there.

00:55:11.541 --> 00:55:13.333
-You don't know that. -[James] Hey, hey, hey.

00:55:13.416 --> 00:55:15.500
Both of you, just chill.

00:55:16.916 --> 00:55:18.583
Okay? We're all going together.

00:55:20.166 --> 00:55:24.541
Honestly, I think what Sara is saying makes a lot of sense.

00:55:24.625 --> 00:55:26.458
Why are you taking her side?

00:55:26.541 --> 00:55:28.375
I'm not taking anyone's side.

00:55:28.458 --> 00:55:30.166
I just want to stick together.

00:55:30.750 --> 00:55:32.416
Are you saying I can't take care of my friends?

00:55:32.500 --> 00:55:34.375
You always do this!

00:55:35.750 --> 00:55:37.208
You twist things!

00:55:37.291 --> 00:55:39.291
I'm tired of it.

00:55:39.375 --> 00:55:41.708
Being with you is tiring.

00:55:46.125 --> 00:55:48.291
-Max, um... -[stifled sobs]

00:55:48.375 --> 00:55:49.958
-It's not like that. I-- -[Max clears throat]

00:55:50.041 --> 00:55:51.541
Okay.

00:55:56.625 --> 00:56:00.333
Then let me make this really easy for the both of you.

00:56:13.333 --> 00:56:14.791
James, no.

00:56:16.291 --> 00:56:17.583
Are you kidding me?

00:56:18.291 --> 00:56:20.500
I can't let her go alone. I'm sorry.

00:56:25.166 --> 00:56:26.208
[sighs]

00:56:26.291 --> 00:56:27.666
You're kidding me.

00:56:28.666 --> 00:56:30.666
[breathing heavily]

00:56:36.041 --> 00:56:37.041
[James] Max.

00:56:38.000 --> 00:56:39.083
James.

00:56:42.291 --> 00:56:43.583
You're coming with me?

00:56:43.666 --> 00:56:45.500
Of course.

00:56:45.583 --> 00:56:47.208
[Sara] Ocean outlet's right there.

00:56:50.583 --> 00:56:54.000
But you're right, we don't know what's on the other side, so we'll try it your way.

00:56:54.083 --> 00:56:56.125
[panting] Okay. Thank you.

00:56:57.666 --> 00:57:00.750
We're in the Skeleton Cave, which connects to the Honeycomb Tunnel.

00:57:00.833 --> 00:57:02.583
Okay. Okay.

00:57:02.666 --> 00:57:03.666
Let's do it.

00:57:06.750 --> 00:57:08.250
Thank you for trusting me.

00:57:08.333 --> 00:57:09.541
I mean it.

00:57:10.541 --> 00:57:12.541
[atmospheric music playing]

00:57:19.541 --> 00:57:21.958
[Max] Map says there's an underwater entrance here.

00:57:24.375 --> 00:57:26.875
Okay, wait. No one panic.

00:57:26.958 --> 00:57:28.500
I'll go check it out.

00:57:33.416 --> 00:57:35.416
[panting quietly]

00:57:37.458 --> 00:57:40.208
Look, I made a call back there.

00:57:40.291 --> 00:57:42.958
We let her go off on her own, how is that any better

00:57:43.041 --> 00:57:44.333
Than what happened to you yesterday?

00:57:44.416 --> 00:57:46.166
Because I'm not the one who swam away.

00:57:46.250 --> 00:57:48.916
I'm the one who got left behind.

00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:51.041
Don't pretend like you're not part of the problem, too.

00:57:51.125 --> 00:57:52.500
What does that mean?

00:57:52.583 --> 00:57:54.416
You let her be in charge.

00:57:56.375 --> 00:57:58.916
[Max breathing heavily]

00:58:00.791 --> 00:58:02.625
[Max] It's a long breath hold,

00:58:02.708 --> 00:58:04.583
But we can do it.

00:58:05.583 --> 00:58:07.916
I'm safe. I'm special. I'm me.

00:58:15.375 --> 00:58:16.625
Ladies first.

00:58:22.375 --> 00:58:24.375
[suspenseful music playing]

00:58:44.375 --> 00:58:46.375
♪ ♪

00:58:55.125 --> 00:58:56.541
Where do we go from here?

00:58:56.625 --> 00:58:59.125
The map says that this cave definitely connects to the entrance,

00:58:59.208 --> 00:59:02.416
But the only way that I can figure it out... is through up there.

00:59:06.333 --> 00:59:08.500
I think the shark's definitely not up there.

00:59:18.500 --> 00:59:19.708
[grunting]

00:59:27.750 --> 00:59:28.750
-[grunts] -[debris falling]

00:59:28.833 --> 00:59:30.208
[gasps]

00:59:33.750 --> 00:59:36.166
[straining]

00:59:44.041 --> 00:59:45.416
[grunts]

00:59:45.500 --> 00:59:47.625
[panting]

00:59:47.708 --> 00:59:49.375
[straining]

00:59:51.625 --> 00:59:54.041
It's narrow. Like, really narrow.

00:59:55.166 --> 00:59:57.583
-Then we better start crawling. -Okay.

00:59:59.666 --> 01:00:01.958
[rustling]

01:00:02.041 --> 01:00:04.041
[grunting]

01:00:10.791 --> 01:00:13.000
[Sara groans, pants]

01:00:19.875 --> 01:00:21.583
I don't want to die in here.

01:00:22.333 --> 01:00:24.416
None of us want to die, babe.

01:00:24.500 --> 01:00:29.666
No, I mean, I can't die while I'm, like...

01:00:29.750 --> 01:00:32.250
Dicking around in Thailand.

01:00:32.333 --> 01:00:34.125
I can't do that to my parents.

01:00:37.208 --> 01:00:38.791
I wasted my life.

01:00:40.833 --> 01:00:44.791
I should've, I don't know, uh, uh, taken things more seriously

01:00:44.875 --> 01:00:49.875
And not put off growing up until law school.

01:00:50.916 --> 01:00:53.416
What if that's all my mom gets of me?

01:00:56.791 --> 01:00:57.875
Being an idiot.

01:00:58.458 --> 01:00:59.791
You're not an idiot.

01:00:59.875 --> 01:01:01.208
Not even close.

01:01:01.291 --> 01:01:03.250
I wasted so much time.

01:01:04.416 --> 01:01:06.541
[Sara] We're gonna get out of here.

01:01:08.166 --> 01:01:10.458
We just got to keep moving.

01:01:12.541 --> 01:01:14.541
If I get out of here, I swear I'm gonna--

01:01:14.625 --> 01:01:16.000
[screaming]

01:01:16.083 --> 01:01:18.958
No, no, no! No, no, no!

01:01:19.041 --> 01:01:21.000
[all breathing heavily]

01:01:22.000 --> 01:01:24.250
No. No.

01:01:32.458 --> 01:01:33.833
[grunts]

01:01:35.916 --> 01:01:37.416
What is that?

01:01:37.500 --> 01:01:39.500
[distant chirping]

01:01:40.791 --> 01:01:42.291
Shh!

01:01:44.541 --> 01:01:46.666
-You guys hear that? -[birds chirping]

01:01:46.750 --> 01:01:49.500
[gentle, hopeful music playing]

01:01:52.166 --> 01:01:54.416
Can you turn your light off for a sec?

01:01:54.500 --> 01:01:56.125
[chirping continues]

01:01:57.541 --> 01:01:58.958
[Max] Is-is that...

01:01:59.041 --> 01:02:01.041
[laughing] Is that daylight?

01:02:01.125 --> 01:02:03.208
Oh, my God. Oh, my God, go, go, go!

01:02:03.291 --> 01:02:05.375
Let's get the hell out of here! Oh, my God.

01:02:05.458 --> 01:02:06.750
[screams]

01:02:06.833 --> 01:02:08.000
[James yells]

01:02:08.083 --> 01:02:09.375
[pained grunt]

01:02:09.458 --> 01:02:11.125
What do I do? What's underneath me?

01:02:11.208 --> 01:02:13.875
-Hold on to Sara's hand. -No, I can't. She's gonna drop me.

01:02:13.958 --> 01:02:15.375
Stop.

01:02:17.291 --> 01:02:19.291
[tense music playing]

01:02:22.291 --> 01:02:23.916
Don't move.

01:02:31.291 --> 01:02:33.083
[trembling breaths]

01:02:33.166 --> 01:02:35.083
[whimpering]

01:02:36.291 --> 01:02:37.625
[gasps]

01:02:50.583 --> 01:02:53.416
-[gasping, whimpering] -[rocks splashing]

01:02:55.416 --> 01:02:56.416
No.

01:02:56.500 --> 01:02:58.041
[whimpering]

01:03:04.750 --> 01:03:06.958
[Sara] James, stop. It's gonna break.

01:03:08.375 --> 01:03:10.375
[Max continues whimpering]

01:03:12.250 --> 01:03:13.291
-It's gone. -[Max yells]

01:03:13.375 --> 01:03:15.083
Okay, get her up, get her up, get her up!

01:03:15.166 --> 01:03:18.041
-I can't reach. Pull her up. -[Sara] I can't. I can't.

01:03:18.125 --> 01:03:19.291
[grunts]

01:03:19.375 --> 01:03:21.416
-I can't. I can't. -Help. Help me.

01:03:21.500 --> 01:03:23.833
[straining]

01:03:23.916 --> 01:03:25.416
-[yelps] -[Max screams]

01:03:25.500 --> 01:03:27.541
-[sharp, heavy breathing] -I have to let you go.

01:03:27.625 --> 01:03:29.250
No. No, babe, no, no!

01:03:29.333 --> 01:03:31.000
-We're coming with you. -[screams]

01:03:35.833 --> 01:03:38.041
[atmospheric music playing]

01:03:48.416 --> 01:03:51.041
[birds chirping in distance]

01:03:59.500 --> 01:04:00.791
[breathing heavily]

01:04:00.875 --> 01:04:02.291
We got to go. We got to go.

01:04:02.375 --> 01:04:03.458
Okay, hold on.

01:04:03.541 --> 01:04:05.791
Let me just check. Let me look.

01:04:05.875 --> 01:04:07.958
Okay? One second. [inhales deeply]

01:04:25.916 --> 01:04:27.916
[panting]

01:04:29.458 --> 01:04:31.416
Okay.

01:04:31.500 --> 01:04:33.708
There's a tunnel down here.

01:04:33.791 --> 01:04:36.000
And it has an air pocket, and I can see it,

01:04:36.083 --> 01:04:39.791
But then we have to hold our breath and swim to the air pocket.

01:04:39.875 --> 01:04:41.416
Do you think we can do it?

01:04:41.500 --> 01:04:43.125
There's no other choice.

01:04:44.208 --> 01:04:45.666
We can do it.

01:04:47.916 --> 01:04:49.083
All right.

01:04:52.708 --> 01:04:54.708
[tense, atmospheric music playing]

01:05:20.541 --> 01:05:22.416
[gasping]

01:05:23.541 --> 01:05:26.500
That felt like... like a long breath hold.

01:05:26.583 --> 01:05:28.500
There's not a lot of air in here.

01:05:28.583 --> 01:05:30.416
Try not to talk so much.

01:05:30.500 --> 01:05:32.541
I'm gonna swim ahead, see how far it goes.

01:05:32.625 --> 01:05:34.375
[inhales deeply]

01:05:36.458 --> 01:05:38.666
-Max. -Hmm?

01:05:38.750 --> 01:05:39.916
If we don't--

01:05:40.000 --> 01:05:42.583
Don't even... don't even say that.

01:05:42.666 --> 01:05:45.250
Don't even think that, okay? W-We're gonna get out of here.

01:05:48.041 --> 01:05:50.875
Okay, the whole tunnel has air pockets, little breaks in the ceiling.

01:05:50.958 --> 01:05:52.916
Okay, so...

01:05:53.000 --> 01:05:55.833
Yeah, we... we swim to the next one and the next one.

01:05:55.916 --> 01:05:57.916
Okay? Let's do it.

01:05:58.000 --> 01:05:59.750
-[Sara inhales deeply] -Be like the shark.

01:05:59.833 --> 01:06:01.000
Never stop moving.

01:06:01.083 --> 01:06:02.750
[Max takes deep breath, whimpers softly]

01:06:02.833 --> 01:06:04.333
[inhales deeply]

01:06:05.541 --> 01:06:07.541
[suspenseful music playing]

01:06:11.458 --> 01:06:14.000
[groaning]

01:06:18.500 --> 01:06:21.500
[gasping]

01:06:25.125 --> 01:06:27.125
♪ ♪

01:06:48.166 --> 01:06:50.166
♪ ♪

01:06:58.000 --> 01:06:59.291
[muffled scream]

01:06:59.375 --> 01:07:01.583
[intense music playing]

01:07:13.750 --> 01:07:16.041
[muffled shouting]

01:07:18.333 --> 01:07:21.208
[breathing heavily]

01:07:21.291 --> 01:07:23.416
Go, go, go!

01:07:23.500 --> 01:07:25.083
[inhales deeply]

01:07:32.666 --> 01:07:34.416
[muffled screaming]

01:07:50.750 --> 01:07:52.958
[muffled screaming]

01:07:59.833 --> 01:08:02.458
[gasping]

01:08:02.541 --> 01:08:04.500
-[James] No air. -[Max] Keep going.

01:08:07.416 --> 01:08:08.958
[inhales deeply]

01:08:11.458 --> 01:08:13.458
[atmospheric music playing]

01:08:20.957 --> 01:08:23.375
-[jarring, intense music playing] -[muffled whimpering]

01:08:37.791 --> 01:08:39.791
[atmospheric music playing]

01:08:48.832 --> 01:08:50.666
[rock rumbling]

01:08:52.875 --> 01:08:55.375
[muffled, urgent grunting]

01:08:59.875 --> 01:09:02.500
[breathing deeply]

01:09:10.957 --> 01:09:13.082
[breathing heavily]

01:09:17.625 --> 01:09:19.666
[muffled grunting]

01:09:40.791 --> 01:09:42.125
I love you.

01:09:43.207 --> 01:09:45.166
-[mournful music playing] -[muffled whimpering]

01:09:46.250 --> 01:09:47.500
Keep moving.

01:09:52.166 --> 01:09:54.291
[muffled straining]

01:09:56.375 --> 01:09:58.458
[grunting]

01:10:03.916 --> 01:10:05.125
[gulps]

01:10:05.208 --> 01:10:07.666
[rapid, sharp breaths]

01:10:25.416 --> 01:10:26.916
[sobbing] Sara!

01:10:28.541 --> 01:10:30.208
No, James!

01:10:31.041 --> 01:10:33.166
-No. -We have to keep moving.

01:10:33.250 --> 01:10:35.375
No, he's... he's right there.

01:10:35.458 --> 01:10:38.916
-We have to keep moving. We do. -No. No.

01:10:39.000 --> 01:10:40.250
I can't. No.

01:10:41.541 --> 01:10:42.625
You and me.

01:10:42.708 --> 01:10:44.583
No. No! [whimpering]

01:10:44.666 --> 01:10:46.791
-We have to keep going. -I don't want-- No, I don't want to.

01:10:46.875 --> 01:10:49.375
We're gonna make it. We're gonna make it.

01:10:49.458 --> 01:10:52.041
One, two...

01:11:13.791 --> 01:11:15.500
[screams, gasps]

01:11:15.583 --> 01:11:17.750
Jesus! Oh, my God.

01:11:23.000 --> 01:11:25.625
-It was in here. -What? [whimpers]

01:11:28.291 --> 01:11:30.500
-[both screaming] -[intense music playing]

01:11:30.583 --> 01:11:32.083
Oh, my God!

01:11:32.166 --> 01:11:35.000
[frantic whimpering, screaming]

01:11:43.666 --> 01:11:45.833
[Max sobbing]

01:11:53.958 --> 01:11:55.958
[hyperventilating]

01:11:58.041 --> 01:12:00.500
We got to go. We got to go.

01:12:07.041 --> 01:12:08.541
[inhales deeply]

01:12:11.250 --> 01:12:13.250
[atmospheric music playing]

01:12:35.916 --> 01:12:37.916
[gasping]

01:12:39.083 --> 01:12:41.208
Okay, get out of the water.

01:12:41.291 --> 01:12:43.375
[both breathing heavily]

01:12:46.333 --> 01:12:48.000
[grunting]

01:12:54.833 --> 01:12:56.833
[tense music playing]

01:13:03.125 --> 01:13:04.208
[screams]

01:13:07.375 --> 01:13:10.791
That's the Ledge Cave, where we lost Adrienne.

01:13:10.875 --> 01:13:12.500
That's the Devil's Mouth.

01:13:13.708 --> 01:13:15.125
[bats squeaking]

01:13:16.041 --> 01:13:17.708
And that's the ocean outlet.

01:13:25.750 --> 01:13:28.250
[shuddering breaths]

01:13:28.333 --> 01:13:30.166
We're right back where we started.

01:13:30.958 --> 01:13:33.083
[screaming]

01:13:38.500 --> 01:13:40.250
[whimpers]

01:13:43.041 --> 01:13:45.166
[sobbing, hyperventilating]

01:13:58.375 --> 01:14:00.166
[burbling]

01:14:04.708 --> 01:14:06.166
What are you doing?

01:14:06.250 --> 01:14:08.250
I'm taking only what we need.

01:14:11.375 --> 01:14:14.583
Are you blaming me for James?

01:14:14.666 --> 01:14:16.041
[melancholy music playing]

01:14:16.125 --> 01:14:17.500
[Max sobs softly]

01:14:18.541 --> 01:14:19.666
No.

01:14:19.750 --> 01:14:21.875
I tried to save him.

01:14:21.958 --> 01:14:24.458
I-I was pulling, and I was pulling and pulling and--

01:14:24.541 --> 01:14:27.125
I know. I know you did.

01:14:29.250 --> 01:14:30.458
I loved him.

01:14:30.541 --> 01:14:32.791
-[Max sobbing] -I loved him, too.

01:14:38.250 --> 01:14:39.625
I know.

01:14:43.250 --> 01:14:45.208
But we tried it your way...

01:14:46.791 --> 01:14:48.916
...and we're back to where we started.

01:14:49.916 --> 01:14:51.750
The exit is right there, Sara.

01:14:51.833 --> 01:14:54.125
-[splashing nearby] -[gasps]

01:14:54.208 --> 01:14:56.041
Shh. Stay here.

01:14:58.375 --> 01:15:00.166
-No, Sara. -I'll check it out.

01:15:00.250 --> 01:15:01.791
No. No.

01:15:01.875 --> 01:15:03.958
[sobbing]

01:15:07.916 --> 01:15:10.916
-[tense, atmospheric music playing] -[bats squeaking]

01:15:16.666 --> 01:15:19.125
-[wings fluttering] -[squeaking continues]

01:15:20.916 --> 01:15:22.833
[jarring, intense music playing]

01:15:22.916 --> 01:15:25.166
[bats squeaking frantically]

01:15:34.833 --> 01:15:35.833
[gasps]

01:15:38.000 --> 01:15:40.500
-What are you doing? -That's the Blue Tunnel.

01:15:40.583 --> 01:15:41.583
That's the exit.

01:15:42.708 --> 01:15:44.125
Get back.

01:15:51.750 --> 01:15:53.750
[tense, atmospheric music playing]

01:15:56.041 --> 01:15:57.958
[trembling breaths]

01:15:58.041 --> 01:16:00.250
[bats shrieking]

01:16:02.916 --> 01:16:04.333
Freeze.

01:16:04.416 --> 01:16:06.083
I don't want it to see you.

01:16:07.625 --> 01:16:09.625
[bats squeaking]

01:16:09.708 --> 01:16:12.958
[Max shudders, whimpers]

01:16:13.833 --> 01:16:15.125
Where is it?

01:16:17.291 --> 01:16:19.416
-[gasping] -Shh.

01:16:22.875 --> 01:16:24.875
[Max whimpering softly]

01:16:26.166 --> 01:16:28.166
[atmospheric music playing]

01:16:29.583 --> 01:16:31.583
[breathing heavily]

01:16:42.583 --> 01:16:45.416
I-I can't tell the path. It's too dark.

01:16:47.458 --> 01:16:49.166
Okay. Turn your light on.

01:16:51.208 --> 01:16:52.291
But just briefly, okay?

01:16:52.375 --> 01:16:54.833
I don't want it to see us if it's still in here.

01:17:00.500 --> 01:17:02.958
[Max breathing heavily]

01:17:12.500 --> 01:17:13.875
[whimpers]

01:17:17.125 --> 01:17:18.958
-What are you doing? -[gasps]

01:17:19.041 --> 01:17:21.041
-I need to see the way. -Turn it off.

01:17:41.750 --> 01:17:44.000
[breath trembling]

01:17:52.916 --> 01:17:55.041
[gasping breaths]

01:18:09.916 --> 01:18:12.166
[tense music playing]

01:18:12.250 --> 01:18:14.333
[screaming]

01:18:14.416 --> 01:18:16.208
-Shh! -[muffled shriek]

01:18:16.291 --> 01:18:17.875
Don't move.

01:18:19.750 --> 01:18:21.375
[whispers] Adrienne.

01:18:22.375 --> 01:18:23.416
Oh, no.

01:18:24.625 --> 01:18:25.708
[Max whimpers]

01:18:28.833 --> 01:18:30.250
You see that spot there?

01:18:30.333 --> 01:18:32.166
We're gonna hide in the stalagmites until it leaves.

01:18:32.250 --> 01:18:35.166
We can't let it follow us into the tunnel.

01:18:35.250 --> 01:18:36.958
We can't.

01:18:38.041 --> 01:18:40.041
[tense, atmospheric music playing]

01:18:41.875 --> 01:18:43.875
[panting]

01:18:46.916 --> 01:18:49.083
Max, stop.

01:18:49.166 --> 01:18:50.791
No, no. Almost there. So close.

01:18:50.875 --> 01:18:52.666
Goddamn it.

01:18:52.750 --> 01:18:54.875
[loud, gasping breaths]

01:18:58.833 --> 01:19:00.708
Max!

01:19:00.791 --> 01:19:02.125
Look!

01:19:02.208 --> 01:19:05.041
-[intense music playing] -[screaming]

01:19:05.125 --> 01:19:06.958
Go! Go, go!

01:19:07.041 --> 01:19:09.041
[screaming continues]

01:19:14.916 --> 01:19:16.500
Hey!

01:19:18.791 --> 01:19:21.250
[Max sobbing]

01:19:29.583 --> 01:19:31.333
[screams, sobs]

01:19:35.375 --> 01:19:36.541
Over here!

01:19:36.625 --> 01:19:38.250
[Max screams]

01:19:40.166 --> 01:19:41.291
[screams]

01:19:41.375 --> 01:19:43.291
No, no!

01:19:44.875 --> 01:19:47.166
[sobs, screams]

01:19:47.250 --> 01:19:49.041
[gasping]

01:19:53.375 --> 01:19:55.250
[Sara screams]

01:19:55.333 --> 01:19:57.791
Over here! Hey!

01:19:58.416 --> 01:20:01.541
Hey! I'm over here!

01:20:06.416 --> 01:20:07.916
[growling]

01:20:26.583 --> 01:20:28.791
-Oh, my God. -We're so close.

01:20:29.291 --> 01:20:31.583
[groans, pants]

01:20:31.666 --> 01:20:32.875
-Can you swim? -[groans]

01:20:32.958 --> 01:20:35.250
-We're-we're... we're trapped. -It's okay.

01:20:35.333 --> 01:20:36.541
We go to the ocean outlet.

01:20:36.625 --> 01:20:38.833
[voice fading] If we go now, we can make it before...

01:20:38.916 --> 01:20:41.166
[disorienting music playing]

01:20:41.250 --> 01:20:43.250
[muffled splash, burbling]

01:20:45.000 --> 01:20:47.000
[atmospheric music playing]

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:02.000
♪ ♪

01:21:05.666 --> 01:21:07.666
[bats squeaking]

01:21:20.458 --> 01:21:22.458
[both grunting]

01:21:22.541 --> 01:21:24.541
[Max] Where-where is it?

01:21:25.500 --> 01:21:27.000
Dead, I hope.

01:21:27.083 --> 01:21:29.083
[pained whimpering]

01:21:30.583 --> 01:21:33.041
[panting]

01:21:39.833 --> 01:21:44.000
We're not moving to L.A., are we?

01:21:57.166 --> 01:21:58.958
We're still here.

01:22:03.416 --> 01:22:06.041
And once we get out of here,

01:22:06.125 --> 01:22:10.166
We can do whatever we want and go wherever we want,

01:22:10.250 --> 01:22:14.583
And we will have all the time in the world...

01:22:16.041 --> 01:22:18.250
...to figure out how to live with this.

01:22:24.291 --> 01:22:26.083
And therapy.

01:22:26.166 --> 01:22:27.166
[Sara chuckles softly]

01:22:27.250 --> 01:22:29.833
New York is probably better for therapists.

01:22:36.125 --> 01:22:38.291
Keep a lookout, okay?

01:22:38.375 --> 01:22:39.666
[Max] Mm-hmm.

01:22:41.958 --> 01:22:43.125
Okay.

01:22:51.041 --> 01:22:53.041
[tense music playing]

01:23:03.750 --> 01:23:05.291
[yells]

01:23:05.375 --> 01:23:07.000
[panting]

01:23:08.458 --> 01:23:10.583
[strains, yells]

01:23:11.791 --> 01:23:14.083
[breathing heavily]

01:23:26.500 --> 01:23:27.958
[pained grunt]

01:23:37.500 --> 01:23:39.500
[yells]

01:23:39.583 --> 01:23:40.666
[grunts]

01:23:40.750 --> 01:23:41.958
[gasping breaths]

01:23:42.041 --> 01:23:44.250
[Sara whimpering, panting]

01:23:53.958 --> 01:23:55.958
[birds chirping]

01:23:56.041 --> 01:23:58.291
[calm, hopeful music playing]

01:24:03.750 --> 01:24:05.750
[ominous music playing]

01:24:13.875 --> 01:24:15.708
Damn.

01:24:23.291 --> 01:24:25.291
[gentle music playing]

01:24:28.541 --> 01:24:31.083
-What? -It's just all rocks down below.

01:24:31.166 --> 01:24:33.958
[voice shaking] So it-it's over?

01:24:34.041 --> 01:24:36.708
You-you can't just, like, climb down, like, w-with-with your rope?

01:24:36.791 --> 01:24:38.750
It's not long enough.

01:24:38.833 --> 01:24:40.458
It's so...

01:24:40.541 --> 01:24:42.000
[sobbing] Oh, my God.

01:24:42.833 --> 01:24:44.458
You-you said... you said this was gonna work.

01:24:44.541 --> 01:24:46.458
-You said this was gonna work. -Shh. It's okay, it's okay.

01:24:46.541 --> 01:24:49.375
Let me just think a second. It's...

01:24:50.208 --> 01:24:55.291
It's low tide, so if we just wait for the tide to come in, and then we can...

01:24:55.375 --> 01:24:57.458
Climb out in a few hours.

01:25:01.458 --> 01:25:03.000
Right.

01:25:03.083 --> 01:25:04.625
[takes deep breath]

01:25:05.791 --> 01:25:08.291
-I'll go alone, and hopefully, the... -[Max sobs]

01:25:08.375 --> 01:25:11.666
...water is high enough for me to jump.

01:25:16.666 --> 01:25:18.958
What if it isn't?

01:25:20.583 --> 01:25:22.791
Then I...

01:25:22.875 --> 01:25:25.166
Break my legs and drown and you die by shark, Max.

01:25:25.250 --> 01:25:26.875
I don't know.

01:25:34.000 --> 01:25:35.541
This'll work.

01:25:38.708 --> 01:25:40.375
This is our best shot.

01:25:40.458 --> 01:25:42.458
[birds chirping in distance]

01:25:54.583 --> 01:25:56.583
[ominous music playing]

01:26:00.750 --> 01:26:01.833
[hissing growl]

01:26:07.875 --> 01:26:09.875
[atmospheric music playing]

01:26:25.708 --> 01:26:27.708
[hopeful music playing]

01:26:36.166 --> 01:26:37.666
[grunts softly]

01:26:44.166 --> 01:26:45.791
[Max] Sara!

01:26:48.291 --> 01:26:50.625
You'll send help, right?

01:26:50.708 --> 01:26:54.458
And I know that we've been through hell, but it's not my fault.

01:26:58.958 --> 01:27:01.000
None of it's my fault.

01:27:03.000 --> 01:27:06.208
God! Don't leave me down here.

01:27:06.291 --> 01:27:08.291
[tense music playing]

01:27:10.333 --> 01:27:12.208
What are you doing? This isn't you!

01:27:12.291 --> 01:27:14.083
People change.

01:27:15.000 --> 01:27:16.666
[inhales sharply]

01:27:22.583 --> 01:27:24.000
[sobbing]

01:27:24.083 --> 01:27:25.291
Hey.

01:27:26.291 --> 01:27:28.125
It's okay. It's just another hour or so.

01:27:28.208 --> 01:27:29.333
What is it?

01:27:35.291 --> 01:27:36.708
[sniffles]

01:27:39.916 --> 01:27:41.125
What?

01:27:41.916 --> 01:27:44.000
I'm gonna die alone down here.

01:27:45.250 --> 01:27:46.666
I know it.

01:27:46.750 --> 01:27:48.750
[soft, mournful music playing]

01:27:50.458 --> 01:27:52.333
[sobbing]

01:27:53.125 --> 01:27:54.500
Hey.

01:27:56.416 --> 01:27:58.125
You and me.

01:27:59.458 --> 01:28:01.750
Till the stars burn out, right?

01:28:04.791 --> 01:28:05.875
[sniffles]

01:28:05.958 --> 01:28:08.083
But you're gonna have to do something

01:28:08.166 --> 01:28:10.500
That neither one of us has ever done before.

01:28:11.583 --> 01:28:14.250
Swim with a broken hand?

01:28:15.250 --> 01:28:16.583
No.

01:28:17.833 --> 01:28:19.375
Trust me.

01:28:35.041 --> 01:28:37.041
[waves rumbling]

01:28:37.125 --> 01:28:39.500
I can hear the waves crashing closer.

01:28:44.416 --> 01:28:46.291
So you'll-you'll send help?

01:28:47.000 --> 01:28:48.958
-Of course I will. -Sara, wait.

01:28:49.041 --> 01:28:52.875
My whole life, I thought I had to be the strong one.

01:28:55.583 --> 01:28:58.500
For my dad, for my friends.

01:29:00.125 --> 01:29:01.958
I thought I had to carry that weight.

01:29:03.291 --> 01:29:05.083
But I never saw you.

01:29:08.041 --> 01:29:10.041
How strong you were.

01:29:11.708 --> 01:29:13.666
And I'm so sorry.

01:29:15.666 --> 01:29:17.750
I am so...

01:29:17.833 --> 01:29:20.125
[crying] I am so very sorry.

01:29:23.291 --> 01:29:25.291
I'm coming back for you.

01:29:30.958 --> 01:29:32.958
[quiet, tense music playing]

01:29:38.500 --> 01:29:40.708
-[grunting] -[waves crashing]

01:29:43.791 --> 01:29:45.791
[panting]

01:29:59.583 --> 01:30:01.583
[determined music playing]

01:30:09.250 --> 01:30:10.500
Wait!

01:30:10.583 --> 01:30:12.000
Please!

01:30:12.083 --> 01:30:15.000
What? What are you doing?

01:30:15.083 --> 01:30:16.791
Get back to the rock!

01:30:16.875 --> 01:30:18.541
I-I'm coming with you.

01:30:18.625 --> 01:30:20.375
You can't. Your hand.

01:30:20.458 --> 01:30:21.916
I'll come back for you.

01:30:22.000 --> 01:30:23.208
[grunts]

01:30:23.291 --> 01:30:25.291
I can do this, Max.

01:30:25.375 --> 01:30:27.000
Please, don't leave me.

01:30:30.833 --> 01:30:33.208
[sighs, sniffles]

01:30:34.666 --> 01:30:36.416
Can you get up here?

01:30:37.416 --> 01:30:39.833
[grunting]

01:30:39.916 --> 01:30:41.625
[yelps]

01:30:43.000 --> 01:30:44.208
[gasping]

01:30:44.291 --> 01:30:45.666
[Sara] Okay, hold on.

01:30:45.750 --> 01:30:47.666
[panicked whimpering, gasping]

01:30:48.958 --> 01:30:51.083
Help. [whimpers]

01:30:51.166 --> 01:30:52.833
Go, grab the rope.

01:30:52.916 --> 01:30:54.750
Just tie it around your waist and knot it.

01:30:55.500 --> 01:30:56.958
As tight as you can.

01:30:57.041 --> 01:30:59.041
[waves crashing]

01:30:59.125 --> 01:31:01.166
[dramatic music playing]

01:31:15.375 --> 01:31:17.125
[exhales sharply]

01:31:22.666 --> 01:31:23.666
[Max whimpers]

01:31:23.750 --> 01:31:24.875
-Okay. -Ready?

01:31:24.958 --> 01:31:26.416
[panting] Yeah.

01:31:26.500 --> 01:31:27.500
Start climbing.

01:31:31.416 --> 01:31:33.541
[pained grunting]

01:31:34.541 --> 01:31:35.666
[whimpers]

01:31:42.083 --> 01:31:43.333
[panting] Okay.

01:31:43.416 --> 01:31:45.208
Okay. Okay. [whimpers]

01:31:47.208 --> 01:31:48.333
[screams]

01:31:49.666 --> 01:31:51.250
My feet keep slipping!

01:31:51.333 --> 01:31:52.625
All right.

01:31:53.625 --> 01:31:55.125
Try again.

01:31:55.208 --> 01:31:57.208
[whimpering]

01:31:57.291 --> 01:31:58.833
[panting] Okay.

01:32:01.708 --> 01:32:02.875
[groans]

01:32:02.958 --> 01:32:04.041
Okay.

01:32:04.125 --> 01:32:05.958
[panting] Okay.

01:32:06.041 --> 01:32:08.583
[whimpers, groans]

01:32:09.833 --> 01:32:11.041
[straining]

01:32:12.916 --> 01:32:14.458
Okay. [grunts]

01:32:16.500 --> 01:32:19.000
We're doing it, Sara! We're doing it!

01:32:19.083 --> 01:32:20.291
[gasps]

01:32:23.083 --> 01:32:25.083
[screaming]

01:32:28.458 --> 01:32:29.708
[yelps]

01:32:31.166 --> 01:32:32.958
[yells]

01:32:33.041 --> 01:32:35.500
[muffled shouting]

01:32:35.583 --> 01:32:37.583
[tense music playing]

01:32:46.500 --> 01:32:47.750
[yelps]

01:32:55.791 --> 01:32:58.000
[gasping]

01:33:05.208 --> 01:33:06.916
[shudders] Max.

01:33:07.000 --> 01:33:08.666
[whimpers]

01:33:08.750 --> 01:33:11.125
[grunting]

01:33:12.458 --> 01:33:14.375
[breathing heavily]

01:33:14.458 --> 01:33:16.458
[somber music playing]

01:33:21.583 --> 01:33:24.333
[groaning]

01:33:28.750 --> 01:33:30.750
[panting]

01:33:37.416 --> 01:33:39.500
"Respect the caves."

01:33:39.583 --> 01:33:41.541
This is the Skeleton Cave.

01:33:41.625 --> 01:33:44.083
We are guests here. Caves are master.

01:34:03.500 --> 01:34:04.708
[Max] Sara.

01:34:04.791 --> 01:34:06.458
Emergency photo op.

01:34:14.625 --> 01:34:16.625
[grunting, panting]

01:34:24.708 --> 01:34:26.791
-[Wat] This rock very weak. -[screams]

01:34:26.875 --> 01:34:28.541
You cause collapse, we die.

01:34:51.166 --> 01:34:53.166
[muffled splashing]

01:35:02.916 --> 01:35:04.458
[splashing]

01:35:12.375 --> 01:35:13.708
Hey!

01:35:15.250 --> 01:35:17.166
Come and get it!

01:35:19.666 --> 01:35:21.500
[splashing]

01:35:23.791 --> 01:35:25.791
[panting]

01:35:39.625 --> 01:35:41.625
[atmospheric music playing]

01:35:45.625 --> 01:35:47.250
Dinnertime.

01:35:50.125 --> 01:35:52.541
[tense music playing]

01:35:53.416 --> 01:35:56.416
[splashing]

01:36:03.541 --> 01:36:05.541
[intense, suspenseful music playing]

01:36:18.083 --> 01:36:19.416
[groans]

01:36:19.500 --> 01:36:22.000
[music fades]

01:36:26.541 --> 01:36:28.166
[splashing]

01:36:32.291 --> 01:36:33.833
Come on!

01:36:33.916 --> 01:36:36.208
[intense, suspenseful music playing]

01:36:36.291 --> 01:36:38.291
Come on!

01:36:43.791 --> 01:36:45.000
[growling]

01:36:49.500 --> 01:36:51.375
[pained grunting]

01:36:54.833 --> 01:36:57.041
-Come on. Get back. -[splashing]

01:36:57.125 --> 01:36:59.583
Come back. One more time. Come back!

01:37:20.083 --> 01:37:21.416
[shark growling]

01:37:26.041 --> 01:37:28.333
[rumbling]

01:37:34.083 --> 01:37:35.708
[groans]

01:37:35.791 --> 01:37:38.416
[somber music playing]

01:37:57.375 --> 01:37:59.875
[gasping]

01:37:59.958 --> 01:38:01.750
[coughs]

01:38:01.833 --> 01:38:03.833
[rapid, trembling breaths]

01:38:07.333 --> 01:38:09.333
[hopeful music playing]

01:38:25.708 --> 01:38:27.708
♪ ♪

01:38:30.500 --> 01:38:31.625
[whimpers]

01:38:31.708 --> 01:38:33.666
[birds chirping]

01:38:33.750 --> 01:38:36.166
[panting, whimpering]

01:38:51.500 --> 01:38:52.791
[sniffles]

01:39:00.166 --> 01:39:01.708
[chuckles]

01:39:03.791 --> 01:39:06.166
[laughs loudly]

01:39:06.250 --> 01:39:08.083
[screams]

01:39:08.166 --> 01:39:11.708
[echoing scream]

01:39:11.791 --> 01:39:13.791
[triumphant music playing]

01:39:29.625 --> 01:39:31.625
[music fades]

01:39:33.500 --> 01:39:35.500
[dramatic music playing]

01:40:05.500 --> 01:40:07.500
♪ ♪

01:40:37.500 --> 01:40:39.500
♪ ♪

01:41:09.500 --> 01:41:11.500
♪ ♪

01:41:41.500 --> 01:41:43.500
♪ ♪

